window.__T__=[{"i":19040,"text":"1: \nA single large glossy sapphire-blue maple leaf, centered and oriented vertically,\n\nits surface like liquid glass / colored enamel: swirling flame-shaped veins glowing\nfrom deep sapphire at the outer edges through royal blue and bright azure to\nice-white at the centre, wet ultra-glossy reflective highlights, 3D embossed look,\na thin slender stem tapering down and ending in a small polished platinum base.\nAround it, near the corners, five smaller metallic platinum maple leaves with\nmirror-polished glossy silver-white surfaces and sharp specular highlights.\nBackground: luxurious white satin silk fabric with soft flowing drapery folds\nand a subtle silky sheen; a few small glossy pearl beads scattered on the fabric.\nSoft diffused studio lighting from above, elegant premium product-shot aesthetic,\nultra detailed, hyper-realistic 3D render, \ntext, letters, watermark, logo, signature, frame, border, ornate edging,\nextra red leaves, matte or dull colours, plastic toy look, blurry, low detail,\ncartoon, flat 2D, harsh shadows, clutter, busy background\n\nPrompt 2:\nA single large maple leaf made of faceted cut crystal / prismatic glass, centered\n\nand oriented vertically, its surface divided into sharp geometric triangular facets\nlike a shattered gem or a low-poly mosaic, overlaid with a holographic iridescent\nfilm that shifts through emerald green, teal, aquamarine, deep jade and soft mint\ndepending on the angle. Thin polished gold veins run through the leaf following the\nnatural maple venation, and several inner panels are filled with fine dotted /\nstippled gold texture. A slender polished gold stem tapers down, ending in a small\nflared golden base.\nAround it, near the four corners, four smaller maple leaves in polished\nwhite-gold / champagne metal with the same emerald-teal holographic gradient\nand gold dotted texture on their surface.\nBackground: white satin silk fabric with soft flowing drapery folds and a silky sheen;\nbright iridescent green, teal and mint caustics and coloured light reflections spilled\nacross the fabric beneath the central leaf.\nSoft bright diffused studio lighting from above, strong sharp specular highlights,\nluxury premium product-shot aesthetic, ultra detailed, hyper-realistic 3D render,\ntext, letters, watermark, logo, signature, frame, border, ornate edging,\nmatte or dull surfaces, opaque plastic toy look, blurry facets, muddy colours,\nflat 2D, cartoon, harsh black shadows, cluttered background, dust, scratches","imgs":["https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HSwaFKrXUAApd3A.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HSwaGZtXwAE9rZ3.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HSwaGanXYAAZVBt.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/tweet_video_thumb/HSwaChtWkAA341g.jpg"]},{"i":19041,"text":"请基于我上传的照片，制作一张独立的 3:4竖版“惊魂片场双生”海报。\n\n画面上下严格 1:1分割。\n\n上半部分\n\n完整保留原始照片。\n\n保持：\n\n同一个人物\n\n同一张脸\n\n同一个动作\n\n同一套服装\n\n同一个场景\n同一个拍摄角度\n同一个构图\n只做轻度统一调色，不改变照片内容。\n下半部分\n严格保持上半部分中的：\n人物身份、面部特征、发型、服装、动作、姿态、主体位置、场景结构和构图不变。\n\n将整个画面重构为一帧 90年代悬疑惊悚电影定格画面。\n\n加入：\n\n昏暗室内光线\n\n冷暖混合灯光\n\nVHS录像带颗粒\n\n轻微色偏\n\n低照度噪点\n微弱镜头模糊\n轻微曝光不稳定\n老式录像质感\n然后在原场景中选择一个合理位置：\n门口 / 走廊 / 镜子 / 窗外 / 楼梯口 / 房间深处 / 停车场远处\n加入一个模糊、距离较远、部分被遮挡的神秘人影。\n要求这个人影：\n\n不抢主体\n\n不遮挡人物\n\n不靠近镜头\n\n不出现血腥元素\n\n不出现具体影视IP角色\n不复制现有恐怖电影人物\n轮廓清晰但五官不可辨认\n必须符合真实空间透视\n必须符合现场光源方向\n像原本就站在场景里\n最终效果必须像：\n原本是一张普通生活照，但后来才发现背景里多了一个不该出现的人。\n禁止：\n禁止换脸\n\n禁止改动作\n\n禁止改变人物年龄\n\n禁止把场景完全换掉\n\n禁止出现血腥\n禁止肢体异常\n禁止怪物贴脸\n禁止夸张鬼脸\n禁止满屏恐怖元素\n禁止做成游戏海报\n禁止明显AI插画感\n🔁延伸玩法\n酒店照\n人在酒店房间里正常拍照。\n下半让走廊尽头、房门缝隙或者镜子里出现一个远处人影。\n很容易出电影截图感。\n旅行照\n\n白天正常景点照。\n\n下半改成傍晚或夜间版本，在远处建筑、树林、长廊里藏一个模糊人影。\n\n特别适合古镇、城堡、酒店、老建筑。\n\n电梯照\n\n原图保持自拍。\n\n下半只让电梯镜面、后方走廊出现一个“不该出现的人”。\n\n这种最适合做细看才发现的效果。\n\n停车场\n\n人物和车辆全部不动。\n\n下半压暗环境，在远处柱子后面加一个半遮挡人影。\n\n很像电影预告片截图。\n\n产品照\n\n也可以不用“人影”。\n\n比如香水、手表、相机，可以让产品背后出现模糊轮廓、长阴影或异常反射，做成悬疑广告。\n\n⚙️参数技巧\n\n1. 人影一定要远\n\n不要让“神秘角色”站到人物旁边。\n\n越远，越像真的。\n\n2. 最好只出现一个\n\n一个人影最有效。\n\n太多就会变成普通恐怖海报。\n\n3. 优先藏在合理位置\n\n最好用：\n\n门口\n\n走廊\n\n镜子\n\n窗外\n\n柱子后面\n楼梯尽头\n不要凭空悬浮。\n4. 不要把画面做太黑\n主体脸还是要看得清。\n建议保持：\n\n主体正常曝光 + 背景逐渐压暗。\n\n5. 想更像老电影，可以补充\n\nVHS grain\n\nanalog video noise\n\nslight chromatic aberration\n\nlow-light photography\n\nsubtle tape distortion\n1990s thriller still\n📌一句话总结\n上传一张普通照片，让AI在背景里偷偷加一个“不该出现的人”。","imgs":["https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HSyCNwNaoAAvp4w.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HSyCNwObkAAHqL3.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HSyCNwSbMAAxRyd.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HSyCNwRbcAASbZL.jpg"]},{"i":19042,"text":"Using the supplied first frame as the exact opening image, generate a 30-second horizontal 4:3 photorealistic summer K-pop music video.\n\nCONCEPT\n\nThe five-member fictional K-pop girl group LUMINA performs with twelve international supporting dancers across three connected public locations in the same European neighborhood:\n\n1. Sunny city plaza\n2. Bright covered food market\n3. Outdoor community basketball court\n\nThe visual tone is joyful, energetic and communal. Camera transitions must make the three locations feel physically connected rather than unrelated scenes.\n\nCHARACTER COUNT LOCK\n\nUse exactly:\n- Five LUMINA members\n- Twelve supporting dancers\n\nNo additional dancers may appear.\n\nBackground pedestrians, market vendors and customers are civilians only. They remain clearly separated from the choreography and never copy the dance.\n\nKeep every LUMINA member consistent:\n- Same face\n- Same hairstyle\n- Same outfit\n- Same body proportions\n- Same accessories\n- Same role in the group\n\nDo not duplicate, merge, replace or transform any performer.\n\nCAMERA STYLE\n\nHorizontal 4:3.\nPolished live-action K-pop cinematography.\nUse a stabilized gimbal, short dolly movements and one gentle crane reveal.\n\nCamera movement should be energetic but readable:\n- Smooth forward pushes\n- Short lateral tracks\n- Motivated close-ups\n- Whip-pan transitions hidden by foreground objects\n- Continuous screen direction\n\nDo not use random camera teleportation, spinning camera, extreme shake or excessive cutting.\n\n0.0–4.0 SECONDS — OPENING GROUP CHOREOGRAPHY\n\nContinue directly from the first frame.\n\nNari drops her raised arm across her chest and initiates the first synchronized sequence.\n\nAll seventeen dancers perform:\n- Two grounded side steps\n- Alternating shoulder hits\n- One upward diagonal arm sweep\n- A clean hip-level hand cross\n- One synchronized head turn toward camera-right\n\nThe camera slowly pushes forward while preserving all five main members in frame.\n\nThe yellow bus remains parked behind them. Background pedestrians continue normal movement.\n\n4.0–7.0 SECONDS — NARI CENTER MOMENT\n\nThe other members step outward by half a meter, opening a clear center lane.\n\nNari advances two short steps toward the camera and performs:\n- Right-hand face frame\n- Quick wrist rotation\n- Chest accent\n- Half-turn\n- Immediate return to face the camera\n\nHer pleated skirt, hair and socks move naturally.\n\nTransition into a chest-up shot without cutting off her hands. She smiles directly into the lens for one beat.\n\nNo slow motion.\n\n7.0–10.0 SECONDS — FORMATION EXPANSION\n\nThe camera pulls back smoothly.\n\nMina and Jiyu move to Nari’s sides while Hana and Seoa close the rear line. The twelve supporting dancers expand outward into a wide semicircle.\n\nThe full group performs:\n- Two bouncing steps\n- Right-arm wave\n- Left-arm wave\n- Fast double hand point\n- One small synchronized jump\n- Clean wide-stance landing\n\nFeet maintain accurate contact with the stone pavement.\n\nThe city bus begins moving slowly out of the background in the correct traffic direction.\n\n10.0–12.0 SECONDS — MARKET TRANSITION\n\nA supporting dancer in a cobalt overshirt crosses close to the camera from left to right.\n\nHis shirt briefly fills the frame and creates a natural wipe transition.\n\nAs the blue fabric clears, reveal the same forward camera movement continuing inside a bright covered municipal food market.\n\nThe transition must preserve movement direction and rhythm.\n\n12.0–16.0 SECONDS — MOVING THROUGH THE MARKET\n\nThe five LUMINA members dance forward through a wide central market aisle.\n\nFormation:\n- Jiyu leads at center\n- Nari and Mina follow behind\n- Hana and Seoa occupy the outer positions\n- Supporting dancers trail in two organized lines\n\nEnvironment:\n- White and pale-blue market counters\n- Fresh fruit and vegetable stalls\n- Flower buckets\n- Closed glass seafood displays\n- Hanging international festival flags\n- Elderly vendors and ordinary shoppers standing safely outside the aisle\n- Bright skylight illumination\n- Clean, dry floor\n\nThe group performs walking choreography:\n- Rhythmic forward steps\n- Alternating elbow pulls\n- Shoulder rolls\n- Overhead hand waves\n- One synchronized direction change around a market column\n\nThe camera tracks backward at matching speed.\n\n16.0–19.0 SECONDS — MINA CLOSE-UP\n\nMina moves toward the front-left side of the formation.\n\nThe camera transitions into a smooth waist-up close-up as she performs:\n- Hand sweep beside her cheek\n- Elbow raised above shoulder level\n- Playful head tilt\n- Quick body roll\n- Direct smile into the lens\n\nNari and Jiyu remain visible behind her in softer focus, continuing simpler choreography.\n\nA row of colorful market flags passes above the frame.\n\n19.0–21.0 SECONDS — SECOND MATCH TRANSITION\n\nMina spins once to her left.\n\nHer pale blue-grey skirt creates a brief circular foreground blur.\n\nMatch the end of the spin with Seoa completing the same turn at an outdoor basketball court.\n\nThe rotation direction, body scale and camera height must remain consistent across the cut.\n\n21.0–25.0 SECONDS — BASKETBALL COURT CHORUS\n\nReveal a sunny outdoor community basketball court approximately one block from the market.\n\nEnvironment:\n- Blue and coral painted court\n- White boundary lines\n- Blue basketball backboard\n- Chain-link perimeter fence\n- Colorful city buildings in the distance\n- Green trees\n- Clear afternoon sky\n- No active basketball players inside the dance zone\n\nAll five LUMINA members return to the front row.\nThe twelve supporting dancers form two staggered rows behind them.\n\nThey perform a high-energy chorus:\n- Wide side step\n- Double forearm hit\n- Alternating knee lifts\n- Cross-body point\n- Fast shoulder bounce\n- Quarter-turn\n- Return to front\n\nThe camera tracks laterally from left to right while maintaining a stable horizon.\n\n25.0–28.0 SECONDS — ROTATING CENTER POSITIONS\n\nEach member receives a brief movement highlight without stopping the group choreography:\n\n- Hana performs a grounded two-count footwork accent\n- Seoa performs a bright arm circle\n- Jiyu performs a strong chest-and-shoulder hit\n- Mina performs a face-framing gesture\n- Nari returns to center with one clean pivot\n\nThe other performers stay in their assigned positions and use simplified supporting movements.\n\nNo member passes directly through another dancer’s path.\n\n28.0–30.0 SECONDS — FINAL GROUP POSE\n\nThe camera rises gently by approximately one meter while moving slightly backward, revealing the full court formation.\n\nAll seventeen dancers complete:\n- One synchronized upward arm throw\n- Small controlled jump\n- Stable landing\n- Final asymmetrical pose\n\nFinal positions:\n- Nari center front\n- Mina and Jiyu one step behind her\n- Hana and Seoa on the outer front diagonals\n- Twelve supporting dancers in a broad semicircle\n\nNari looks directly into the camera and gives a bright confident smile.\n\nHold the final pose for the last half-second.\n\nCHOREOGRAPHY QUALITY\n\n- Professional K-pop synchronization\n- Energetic but anatomically realistic movement\n- Clear preparation before every turn and jump\n- Accurate foot placement\n- Natural knee compression on landings\n- Realistic hair and fabric movement\n- No repeated movement loops\n- No performer colliding with another\n- No bodies passing through one another\n- No floating feet\n- No excessive motion blur\n\nSCENE CONTINUITY\n\nAll three locations exist in the same neighborhood and share the same afternoon weather.\n\nMaintain:\n- Consistent sunlight direction\n- Consistent performer identities\n- Consistent clothing\n- Consistent hair\n- Continuous movement direction during transitions\n- Realistic travel logic between scenes\n\nAUDIO\n\nCreate an original upbeat summer K-pop track:\n- Bright percussion\n- Clean bass line\n- Rhythmic handclaps\n- Light synth melody\n- Energetic chorus\n- Original non-lyrical vocal ad-libs\n\nMix in subtle location ambience:\n- Distant city traffic\n- Footsteps\n- Market room tone\n- Shoe contact on the basketball court\n- Light crowd reaction at the final pose\n\nNo recognizable copyrighted melody.\nNo spoken narration.\nNo loud artificial sound effects.\n\nREALISM\n\nThe video should feel like a high-budget K-pop video genuinely filmed in active public locations.\n\nUse:\n- Natural sunlight\n- Real human skin texture\n- Slight perspiration after dancing\n- Realistic clothing wrinkles\n- Physically correct shadows\n- Real architecture\n- Believable civilian reactions\n- Controlled professional camera operation\n\nNEGATIVE CONSTRAINTS\n\nNo extra dancers, missing members, cloned faces, duplicated bodies, identity drift, changing hairstyles, changing outfits, disappearing accessories, skirt transformation, wardrobe malfunction, excessive exposure, merged limbs, extra fingers, broken joints, floating shoes, sliding feet, dancers passing through each other, unstable buildings, duplicated buses, distorted market counters, changing basketball court lines, artificial crowd multiplication, excessive saturation, blown highlights, plastic skin, slow motion, speed ramps, spinning camera, random aerial shot, anime, cartoon, CGI look, subtitles, captions, logos or watermark.\n\nFINAL OUTPUT\n\n30 seconds.\nHorizontal 4:3.\nPhotorealistic live-action K-pop music video.\nFive original adult female group members.\nTwelve adult supporting dancers.\nBright summer European city.\nCity plaza, covered market and outdoor basketball court.\nSmooth match transitions.\nEnergetic synchronized choreography.\nNatural daylight and realistic public environments.","imgs":["https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2102266784128897024/img/VWxqIlUjowTCdTNa.jpg"]},{"i":19043,"text":"Create a premium vertical travel-journal poster in an exact 50/50 split.\n\nTop 50%: Keep the original reference photo completely real and unchanged same composition, architecture, people, colors, lighting, perspective, and details.\n\nBottom 50%: Transform the same photo into a delicate hand-drawn colored-pencil + watercolor sketch on warm cream paper, with visible pencil strokes, soft washes, subtle paper grain, imperfect outlines, and gentle cross-hatching. Keep every subject recognizable.\n\nAdd elegant handwritten text: “A Beautiful Day” above and “Memories to Keep” below. Minimal, nostalgic, sophisticated travel-magazine aesthetic. No extra objects, no photorealism in the bottom half, exact 50/50 layout.","imgs":["https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HS1DIuDaEAAuzSO.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HS1DJfwaQAAsOw1.jpg"]},{"i":19044,"text":"请基于我上传的一张照片，制作一张3:4竖版高级设计海报。\n\n整体上下分为两个区域，高度严格各占50%。\n\n【上半部分】\n\n完整保留原始照片。\n\n保持主体人物身份、五官、发型、服装、姿态、身体比例、环境、镜头角度、自然光线和原始色彩关系不变。\n\n仅进行轻微高级调色，使画面更接近独立摄影杂志和电影静帧质感。\n\n不要改变人物，不要新增人物，不要重新摆姿势。\n\n【下半部分】\n\n仍然基于上半部分的同一张照片、同一个人物和同一个瞬间。\n\n将原始画面重新拆解为3个连续的电影感视觉切片。\n\n三个切片必须来自同一人物、同一环境、同一时间，不要重新生成完全不同的动作。\n\n三个切片建议分别表现：\n\n切片A：\n人物眼神、面部或头部局部特写。\n突出情绪和表情细节。\n\n切片B：\n人物半身或中景。\n保留主体姿态、服装和环境关系，作为主要叙事镜头。\n\n切片C：\n手部、服装、随身物件、鞋子、头发、首饰、产品或环境关键细节特写。\n用细节补充人物状态。\n\n三个切片可以采用横向长条、非等高条带或轻微错位排列，但必须保持清晰秩序。\n\n所有切片保持：\n同一色调\n同一光线方向\n同一摄影质感\n同一人物身份\n\n加入轻微胶片颗粒、电影摄影色彩、自然景深和克制的高光溢出。\n\n画面整体像：\n一张真实照片被自动拆解成3个连续电影镜头。\n\n避免：\n三张完全不同的照片\n人物身份漂移\n重新换衣服\n新增人物\n夸张表情\n复杂拼贴\n贴纸\n多余装饰\n卡通化\n廉价电影滤镜\n\n最关键的一句是：\n\n“三个切片必须来自同一张照片、同一个人物、同一个瞬间。”\n\n📌 一句话总结\n\n三镜情绪切片双生最实用的地方，就是只上传一张照片，就能把一个普通瞬间自动拆成一组有特写、有中景、有细节的电影画面。","imgs":["https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HS3vZfEaMAADXbt.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HS3vZfFb0AEfCG2.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HS3vZfFboAAvxNm.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HS3vZfIagAAxORx.jpg"]},{"i":19045,"text":"Use the uploaded photo as the exact visual reference and transform it into a nostalgic editorial scrapbook-style artwork. Preserve the subjects, composition, clothing, poses, objects, and overall scene from the original photo.\n\nCreate a vertical 3:4 composition with a refined, minimalist Japanese-inspired photo-to-illustration aesthetic.\n\nThe final design should be divided into two equal horizontal sections:\n\nTOP HALF — ORIGINAL PHOTOGRAPH\n•Place the uploaded original photograph in the upper 50% of the canvas.\n•Keep it photorealistic and completely unchanged.\n•Preserve the exact facial features, body proportions, clothing, hairstyle, pose, lighting, environment, furniture, food, blanket, window, and all other recognizable details.\n•Do not crop important subjects.\n•Use the original image naturally, with clean edges and no artificial frame.\n\nBOTTOM HALF — MINIATURE STORYBOOK VERSION\n•Recreate the exact same scene from the photograph as a small, delicate hand-painted illustration positioned around the center of the lower half.\n•Keep the same subjects, poses, clothing, objects, perspective, and recognizable composition, but make the entire scene appear like a tiny nostalgic illustration placed on paper.\n•Use a soft watercolor + colored-pencil + subtle gouache aesthetic.\n•Delicate imperfect brushwork, lightly textured edges, soft shadows, muted natural colors, slightly faded vintage appearance.\n•The miniature scene should occupy only about 25–35% of the lower section, leaving generous negative space around it.\n•Make it feel like a tiny memory captured on paper rather than a conventional full-frame illustration.\n•Add a very subtle hand-drawn shadow underneath the miniature scene to make it feel naturally placed on the paper.\n\nBACKGROUND\n•Cover the entire bottom half with warm off-white / ivory handmade paper.\n•Visible fine paper fibers and subtle grain.\n•Slightly uneven organic texture, similar to premium watercolor paper.\n•Minimal, warm, calm and elegant.\n•No borders, no decorative patterns, no unnecessary elements.\n\nTEXT\n•Beneath the miniature illustration, add a very small handwritten phrase:\n“sunny days”\n•Use thin, delicate, lowercase handwritten script.\n•Light gray/taupe ink.\n•Keep the text subtle and understated, centered beneath the artwork.\n\nLIGHTING & COLOR\n•Warm natural daylight.\n•Soft cream, beige, pale blue, muted denim blue and warm brown tones.\n•Gentle highlights and soft shadows.\n•Slightly nostalgic film-inspired color grading.\n•Avoid oversaturation.\n•Overall mood: quiet, cozy, sentimental, peaceful family memory.\n\nIMPORTANT\n•Maintain the identity and visual characteristics of the people from the reference photo.\n•Do not invent additional people or objects.\n•Do not change clothing or poses.\n•Do not distort anatomy.\n•The miniature illustration must clearly depict the same exact moment and scene as the original photograph.\n•Clean premium editorial composition.\n•High detail, sophisticated art direction, realistic paper texture, subtle handcrafted imperfections.\n•No extra text, no frame, no logo, no watermark.","imgs":["https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HS3za9wasAApSw7.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HS3zbxpbgAA8CBF.jpg"]},{"i":19046,"text":"x 优化 \n\n提示词 ⤵️\n```\n请将我上传的每一张照片分别制作成一张独立的高级极简设计海报，不多图拼接，每张照片单独输出。\n整体采用3:4竖版构图，上下两个区域高度严格1:1，各占画面50%。\n\n上半部分保留原始照片，保持主体结构、真实质感、自然光影和原有色彩氛围，仅进行轻微高级调色，使其具有艺术摄影和展览视觉质感。为适配画幅，可以自然扩展环境背景，但不得拉伸、扭曲或改变主体。\n\n下半部分提取照片中主体最具识别性的轮廓、结构、空间关系与叙事特征，重构为 layered paper cut art / 3D papercraft diorama / architectural relief 风格的纸雕微缩场景。不要复制照片细节，而是保留最核心的视觉符号，通过多层纸片、切割轮廓、镂空结构和空间叠层重新表达，使主体像一件现代设计展览中的纸艺装置。\n\n使用简洁结构、精准边缘、多层切面和轻微空间阴影建立立体感，不追求真实3D渲染，而呈现纸张、建筑模型与艺术装置结合的轻盈质感。主体保持单一视觉中心，大面积留白，构图克制平衡。\n\n配色从上方照片中提取最明亮、最鲜活、最有生命力的颜色重新调制，而不是平均取色。整体提高明度与色彩纯净度，采用清澈天空蓝、湖水青、嫩绿、暖黄、珊瑚橙、桃粉等由原图自然推导出的明快色相，并以象牙白、暖米色作为主要空间背景，通过清爽冷暖关系形成治愈感。主色鲜明但不刺眼，局部暖橙、金黄或粉红作为点睛色。避免灰脏、发旧、低沉莫兰迪化、暗褐滤镜、荧光色和廉价糖果感。\n\n文字少量介入，根据主体、地点、情绪或文化含义自由生成简短标题、编号或微型注释。字体使用细致、克制、具有建筑编辑感的现代字体，像艺术展签或高级品牌视觉中的信息标注，与留白自然融合。\n\n整体风格参考国际设计工作室、建筑海报、艺术展览视觉和高级品牌视觉系统，呈现纸雕空间、现代东方美学、清透色彩、大面积留白和高级工艺感。避免真实CG、塑料质感、儿童手工感、复杂背景和模板化效果。\n```","imgs":["https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HS6MHuzbwAAhPW-.jpg"]},{"i":19047,"text":"Vintage souvenir box layout. \n\n[ Poster Series - Part 4 ]\n\nPrompt:\n\n{\n  \"style_name\": \"Vintage Souvenir Box Travel Poster\",\n  \"prompt_instruction\": \"Generate a vintage travel poster for {{COUNTRY}}. Automatically populate all country-specific fields (language, capital, currency, coordinates, timezone, 10 iconic souvenirs, 2 famous landmarks, national animal/symbol, signature food or drink, folk craft item, cultural ornament, flag-based accent color) based on real, well-known cultural associations with {{COUNTRY}}. Keep every structural/style element below identical across all countries.\",\n  \"canvas\": {\n    \"aspect_ratio\": \"3:4 portrait\",\n    \"resolution\": \"2048x2731 min\",\n    \"print_style\": \"retro travel/postal collage poster, magazine cover feel\"\n  },\n  \"background\": {\n    \"base_color\": \"#FFFFFF\",\n    \"note\": \"Changed from original cream/kraft tan to pure white — texture must be preserved, only hue is swapped\",\n    \"texture\": [\n      \"subtle paper grain / fiber noise overlay, low opacity (8-12%)\",\n      \"faint aged-paper mottling and soft blotch variation, kept very light so white stays dominant\",\n      \"very light vignette at corners (barely darkened, not gray/brown)\",\n      \"no strong yellowing or sepia cast — texture only, not color tint\"\n    ],\n    \"finish\": \"matte fine-art paper, slight tooth/grain visible on close zoom\"\n  },\n  \"typography\": {\n    \"headline\": {\n      \"text\": \"{{COUNTRY_NAME_UPPERCASE}}\",\n      \"font_style\": \"bold condensed vintage slab-serif / stencil-adjacent letterpress type\",\n      \"color\": \"distressed brick red (#B5432E approx)\",\n      \"texture\": \"heavy ink distress, cracked/worn letterpress texture, uneven ink density, grunge edges\",\n      \"placement\": \"full-width banner across top third, large dominant scale, slightly overlapping top design elements\",\n      \"alignment\": \"center\"\n    },\n    \"tagline\": {\n      \"primary_text\": \"COLLECT MEMORIES NOT THINGS.\",\n      \"secondary_text\": \"{{LOCAL_LANGUAGE_TRANSLATION_OF_TAGLINE}} (native script, shown above or beside English line when {{COUNTRY}} has a non-Latin script)\",\n      \"font_style\": \"small tracked-out uppercase serif or typewriter font\",\n      \"color\": \"dark brown/black ink #3A2E27\",\n      \"placement\": \"top center, above or flanking headline\"\n    },\n    \"supporting_labels\": {\n      \"font_style\": \"vintage typewriter / stamped rubber-stamp lettering, uppercase\",\n      \"color\": \"brick red or dark brown ink, stamp-style uneven pressure texture\",\n      \"used_for\": [\n        \"postal stamps\",\n        \"arrival stamps\",\n        \"coordinates\",\n        \"box captions\",\n        \"footer facts\"\n      ]\n    }\n  },\n  \"top_corner_elements\": {\n    \"left_badge\": {\n      \"shape\": \"circular vintage rubber stamp badge\",\n      \"content\": \"{{COUNTRY_NICKNAME_OR_MOTTO}} (e.g. 'Land of the Rising Sun', 'True North Strong and Free')\",\n      \"style\": \"worn circular stamp outline, small icon in center (wave, bear, leaf, or relevant national symbol)\"\n    },\n    \"left_upper_tag\": {\n      \"content\": \"SOUVENIR BOX SERIES (small postal-style tag with plane icon and postmark wavy lines)\"\n    },\n    \"right_upper_stamp\": {\n      \"shape\": \"rectangular postage stamp illustration\",\n      \"content\": \"hand-painted style landmark of {{COUNTRY}} with cherry-blossom/foliage framing where relevant, small denomination number, country postal code text\"\n    },\n    \"right_arrival_stamp\": {\n      \"shape\": \"rectangular dashed-border passport/customs stamp\",\n      \"content\": \"ARRIVED + {{COUNTRY}} + date (e.g. 20 MAY 2024) + arrival airport code + city name\",\n      \"color\": \"brick red ink, slightly rotated/imperfect stamping\"\n    },\n    \"coordinates_text\": {\n      \"content\": \"{{CAPITAL_CITY_LAT_LONG}}°, formatted as N/S and E/W\",\n      \"placement\": \"top right or top left corner, small red serif text\"\n    }\n  }\n}","imgs":["https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HS7kZRrbIAAScMc.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HS7kZRraMAAELnF.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HS7kZRqbUAAxnS2.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HS7kZRobEAAwIOf.jpg"]},{"i":19048,"text":"Continued:\n\n{\n  \"central_box\": {\n    \"container\": {\n      \"type\": \"open cardboard shipping box, flaps folded outward/back\",\n      \"material\": \"natural kraft brown cardboard, corrugated edge texture visible, slightly worn corners\",\n      \"interior\": \"divided into asymmetric grid compartments (like a wooden/cardboard divided tray), each compartment padded with crinkled kraft tissue paper or shredded paper filling\"\n    },\n    \"compartment_layout\": \"8-10 irregular rectangular compartments of varying size, arranged in a loose grid, realistic studio product-photography lighting with soft shadows\",\n    \"souvenir_items\": {\n      \"count\": 10,\n      \"instruction\": \"Auto-select 10 small realistic 3D souvenir objects that are globally recognized as iconic to {{COUNTRY}} — e.g. a miniature famous landmark model, a traditional doll/figurine, a lucky/folk charm, traditional tableware or drinkware, a native animal plush or figurine, a piece of traditional dress/textile accessory, a food or drink product bottle/jar with realistic label, a folded paper fan or textile craft, a keepsake trinket/keychain, and a traditional hat or uniform item.\",\n      \"render_style\": \"hyper-realistic product photography, studio lit, soft shadows, slight vintage color grade (warm highlights, muted saturation)\",\n      \"numbering\": \"optional small circular numbered tags (1-10) in white/cream circles with thin outline, placed beside select items, matching style used in Canada/China/Italy/England versions\"\n    },\n    \"box_front_caption\": {\n      \"text\": \"{{CAPTION}} e.g. '10 SOUVENIRS. X MOMENTS. 1 JOURNEY.' or 'SOUVENIRS FROM {{COUNTRY}}' or 'SOUVENIRS & STORIES from {{COUNTRY}}'\",\n      \"font_style\": \"bold vintage serif, centered on box's front outer flap\",\n      \"color\": \"dark brown ink on kraft cardboard\"\n    }\n  }\n}","imgs":["https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HS7karGaEAAHbX6.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HS7karHaQAA8jXN.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HS7karHaYAAsfPs.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HS7karna8AAFqxa.jpg"]},{"i":19049,"text":"请基于我上传的照片，制作一张独立的 3:4竖版「夜闪拖影双生」海报，画面上下严格1:1分割。\n\n上半：完整保留原始照片，仅轻微调色。\n\n下半：严格保持同一人物、同一张脸、同一服装、同一动作、同一场景和同一构图，将画面重构为真实的夜间直闪长曝光抓拍。\n\n人物面部和身体核心保持清晰锐利，使用强烈但真实的机顶闪光灯定格主体；背景、路人、车辆、街灯和环境高光沿同一个运动方向形成自然拖影、光轨和轻微残像。\n\n加入真实的低照度噪点、数码相机颗粒、闪光衰减、轻微曝光误差和夜间抓拍质感。\n\n最终像：\n\n人物被闪光灯定格的一瞬间，周围世界还在高速移动。\n\n禁止整张照片模糊、换脸、换动作、复制多个完整人物、乱方向拖影、霓虹特效和明显AI感。\n\n🔁延伸玩法\n\n夜街人像\n人物保持清晰，让车灯、路人和店铺灯光从身后拖过去。\n\n旅行照片\n人在景点不动，让游客、车辆、街道灯光形成流动时间感。\n\n运动照片\n跑步、骑车、滑板都很适合，主体定格，环境强化速度。\n\n汽车照片\n汽车保持锐利，道路和城市灯光高速后移，很容易出广告感。\n\n产品照片\n产品不动，让液体、光线、包装碎片或背景元素形成运动轨迹。\n\n⚙️参数技巧\n\n人物一定要清楚。\n这个玩法不是“把照片弄糊”，而是 主体锐利 + 环境运动。\n\n拖影最好只朝一个方向，比如从右向左或从后向前，越统一越像真实慢门。\n\n夜景可以加入：\n\ndirect flash / slow shutter / motion blur / light trails / low-light grain / candid night photography\n\n如果AI生成了好几个完整的人，补一句：\n\n人物只出现一次，残影只能存在于运动边缘和环境，不生成第二个完整主体。\n\n📌一句话总结\n\n上传一张普通照片，让AI把你定格，把整个世界拖过去。","imgs":["https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HS86A9RawAAUgpc.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HS86A9Ga8AA76JR.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HS86A9IaQAAP6Tu.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HS86A9IbEAAh3yc.jpg"]},{"i":19050,"text":"Create a premium cinematic travel-editorial portrait inspired by vintage passport stamps, airline tickets, and luxury destination postcards.\n\nUse the person from the reference image as the main subject, preserving their facial identity, facial features, skin tone, hairstyle, and natural proportions accurately.\n\nShow the person as a stylish adventurous traveler standing beside a vintage cream-colored suitcase, holding an old passport and several travel documents. They wear an elegant timeless travel outfit with a long flowing coat, comfortable boots, sunglasses, and a subtle scarf moving naturally in the breeze.\n\nInstead of a normal background, transform the entire scene into a sophisticated layered PASSPORT COLLAGE.\n\nBehind the person, blend a large iconic destination landscape, vintage passport stamps, faded boarding-pass typography, airline ticket fragments, postage stamps, handwritten travel notes, tiny destination illustrations, map lines, coordinates, luggage tags, and architectural silhouettes.\n\nCreate the feeling that the person has literally stepped OUT OF A PASSPORT PAGE and into the destination.\n\nPlace a large vintage passport-stamp circle partially behind the person reading:\n“ADVENTURE AWAITS”\n“PASSPORT • 2026”\n\nAdd a realistic boarding pass section at the bottom with:\nDESTINATION: [CITY / COUNTRY]\nGATE: 07\nSEAT: A24\nCLASS: EXPLORER\n\nUse warm ivory paper, faded terracotta, muted teal, antique gold, dusty blue and dark brown instead of the usual bright travel-poster colors.\n\nAdd subtle paper folds, ink bleed, vintage stamps, distressed edges, film grain and authentic printed texture.\n\nThe person remains photorealistic while the surrounding passport elements have a refined vintage editorial illustration quality.\n\n4:5 vertical composition, luxury travel magazine aesthetic, cinematic golden-hour lighting, sophisticated, nostalgic, adventurous, highly detailed, realistic photography blended with premium vintage graphic design.\n\nNo cartoon appearance, no excessive text, no distorted face, no extra limbs, no duplicated person.","imgs":["https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HS9A672a8AA12Fh.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HS9A675bIAAwRax.jpg"]},{"i":19051,"text":"Create a refined editorial travel-art composition based on a reference photograph. The image is divided vertically into two parts: the upper section is a realistic cinematic travel photograph, while the lower section transforms the exact same scene into a delicate hand-painted watercolor illustration.\nUpper section: authentic candid travel photography, natural daylight, soft shadows, subtle film grain, realistic textures, sophisticated European atmosphere, documentary-style composition, people naturally walking through the scene, beautiful architectural details, slightly muted elegant colors, high-end travel magazine photography.\nLower section: a minimalist handmade watercolor painting of the exact same scene, preserving the recognizable composition, architecture, people, poses, perspective and major visual elements from the photograph. Loose translucent watercolor washes, delicate ink details, visible paper texture, soft edges, imperfect brushwork, subtle pigment bleeding, airy negative space, understated pastel tones, artistic but realistic.\nLeave generous warm ivory/off-white textured paper space surrounding the watercolor illustration. Add a small elegant handwritten caption near the bottom, such as “summer days” or “a quiet afternoon”, with a thin minimalist horizontal line underneath.\nOverall aesthetic: luxury travel journal, fine-art watercolor postcard, contemporary editorial design, nostalgic European summer, understated elegance, tactile handmade paper, sophisticated and serene.\nPortrait orientation, clean composition, premium art direction, no clutter, no borders, natural proportions, highly detailed photograph transitioning into an airy watercolor illustration.","imgs":["https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HS9TeoZacAAUkgc.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HS9TetgacAAPcaq.jpg"]},{"i":19052,"text":"Using the supplied reference image as the exact product reference, create an ultra-premium cinematic fashion advertising film for the same fictional burgundy luxury sandal.\n\nPRODUCT CONSISTENCY:\nThe sandal must remain EXACTLY the same throughout the entire sequence. Preserve its deep burgundy/oxblood color, oversized sculptural silhouette, architectural platform sole, asymmetric straps, dark-chrome hardware, stitching, embossed geometric emblem, proportions, materials and construction. Never redesign, morph, duplicate or replace the product.\n\nCONCEPT:\nA futuristic luxury footwear campaign introducing the sandal as an iconic fashion object.\n\nThe film should feel like a global premium fashion advertisement — sophisticated, cinematic, minimal, bold and expensive.\n\nVISUAL STYLE:\nUltra-photorealistic luxury commercial.\nDark futuristic fashion runway.\nGlossy black reflective floor.\nDeep charcoal architectural environment.\nSubtle atmospheric haze.\nBurgundy light accents.\nControlled studio lighting.\nHigh-contrast cinematic exposure.\nPremium editorial color grading.\nRealistic leather and metal reflections.\nExtremely clean visual composition.\n\nCAMERA & MOTION:\nUse constantly evolving premium commercial cinematography:\n\n* Extreme wide establishing shot\n* Low-angle hero shot\n* Slow cinematic dolly-in\n* Smooth lateral tracking shot\n* Macro product detail shot\n* Controlled 90-degree orbit\n* Low-to-high reveal\n* Fast but elegant push-in\n* Slow-motion three-quarter rotation\n* Extreme close-up of leather texture\n* Close-up of dark-chrome hardware\n* Final symmetrical hero composition\n\nAll camera movement must be perfectly stabilized, intentional and physically realistic.\n\nEDITING:\nCreate sophisticated modern commercial editing with precise cuts synchronized to the music.\n\nUse:\n\n* Speed ramps\n* Elegant match cuts\n* Subtle whip transitions\n* Motion-blur transitions\n* Micro zoom transitions\n* Seamless angle changes\n* Short rhythmic cuts\n* Slow-motion moments for product details\n* Clean cinematic fades\n* Brief black-frame impact transitions\n\nNever use cheap, excessive or distracting effects.\n\nKINETIC TYPOGRAPHY / SUBTITLES:\nIntegrate premium animated typography directly into the commercial.\n\nUse minimal elegant typography with modern editorial fashion-advertising aesthetics.\n\nExample on-screen text sequence:\n\n“BUILT TO BE SEEN”\n\nthen:\n\n“SCULPTED IN BURGUNDY”\n\nthen:\n\n“FORM. POWER. PRECISION.”\n\nthen:\n\n“THE NEW ICON”\n\nTypography should animate with subtle tracking expansion, smooth upward movement, masked reveals, kinetic positioning and precise timing with the soundtrack.\n\nText should appear naturally within negative space and NEVER cover important parts of the sandal.\n\nUse clean premium white/off-white typography with extremely subtle burgundy accents.\n\nDo not use recognizable real-world brand typography or logos.\n\nVOICEOVER:\nAdd a deep, sophisticated cinematic voiceover with a calm confident delivery.\n\nVoiceover:\n\n“Some designs are made to be worn.\n\nOthers are made to be remembered.\n\nSculpted with precision.\nDefined by presence.\n\nThis is more than a sandal.\n\nThis is the new icon.”\n\nThe voice should sound like a premium international fashion campaign: restrained, confident, cinematic and sophisticated.\n\nAUDIO DESIGN:\nCreate a complete luxury commercial soundscape.\n\nBegin with a deep atmospheric cinematic tone.\n\nGradually introduce:\n\n* Deep sub-bass\n* Elegant electronic pulse\n* Minimal fashion-show percussion\n* Subtle metallic impacts\n* Soft whooshes during camera movements\n* Cinematic risers before major reveals\n* Sharp impact sound during typography transitions\n* Subtle leather/material foley\n* Spacious reverb\n\nMusic should build toward the final hero shot without overpowering the voiceover.\n\nEDITING RHYTHM:\nStart slow and mysterious.\nBuild tension during the product reveal.\nIncrease cutting speed during the detail sequence.\nBriefly slow down for the final reveal.\nFinish with a powerful clean hero frame.\n\nFINAL HERO:\nEnd on an immaculate low three-quarter hero shot of the exact same burgundy sandal centered on the runway.\n\nThe sandal is illuminated by a controlled overhead spotlight while its reflection appears on the glossy floor.\n\nCamera performs a very subtle final push-in.\n\nDisplay:\n\n“THE NEW ICON”\n\nThen a clean fade to black.\n\nOVERALL FEEL:\nUltra-premium.\nFuturistic.\nFashion-forward.\nMinimal.\nCinematic.\nSophisticated.\nCommercially believable.\nLike a multimillion-dollar luxury footwear campaign.\n\nSTRICTLY AVOID:\nProduct morphing, changing sandal design, changing colors, additional footwear, humans, feet, distorted anatomy, duplicated products, floating objects, random props, excessive VFX, cartoon effects, cheap transitions, illegible typography, flickering text, warped geometry, unrealistic leather, or inconsistent hardware.\n #PixVerseRunway #IMG25onPixVerse","imgs":["https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2102992363417448448/img/m7Ak2MBPUW34Dz20.jpg"]},{"i":19053,"text":"```\n让未来主题先提炼成一个可被阅读的强标题、少量信息行和一套可铺满画面的线性结构；画面第一眼必须是顶部极重、极黑、被裁切般逼近边缘的粗体字块压住下方大面积细线场，标题像建筑横梁而不是装饰字。主体图像不以写实物件出现，而被转译为多组横向、略起伏、手工错位的平行细线，线组之间有断裂、交叉、局部倾斜和不完全对齐，形成可读秩序与即兴失衡并存的底层网格。主题能量通过散落的颜料点、短擦痕和小色块介入线场，颜色采用少数高饱和原色与轻灰、浅粉、浅蓝、绿、橙并置，像印刷后被手工泼洒或误套色留下的痕迹；色点大小悬殊，既有针尖小点也有指腹般斑块，分布看似随机但围绕线的节奏产生停顿、重音和跳跃。文字系统采用极端压缩层级：主标题为厚重无衬线黑块，字形宽阔、笔画均匀、内白被压小、端点平直、连接紧密，任何书写系统都应保持块面优先和正字识别；辅助文字细窄、冷静、贴近标题或底边，作为制度化信息而非视觉主角。背景保持未装饰白纸，保留干净边界、轻微印刷生硬感和手工污点的不完美，不加渐变、阴影、摄影质感、精致插画、对称装饰或柔化美化，让黑色秩序与彩色事故共同构成主题。\n\n——————\n主题：中秋节海报\n\n一共10张\n每张都是不同的基于这个美学dna的不同创意\n```","imgs":["https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HS9W3wTbsAAKIBF.jpg"]},{"i":19054,"text":"STYLE: raw candid smartphone video shot from across the street, looks like a bystander filmed it and posted it. Photorealistic, low contrast, muted desaturated colors, flat overcast daylight, real concrete and asphalt texture, phone sensor noise, slight rolling-shutter wobble on fast moves, focus hunting, digital zoom softness when zoomed in. Handheld level 2 to 3: the camera is a phone held in someone's hands, it bounces with the operator's breathing and small steps, reframing lags behind the action, no smooth gimbal, no stabilization. Everything is real animals with accurate anatomy, size and feather/fur texture. No CGI feel, no cinematic grading.\n\nREFERENCES:\n@Image 1 is the exact FIRST frame, start with no change. Lock everything in it: the grey feral pigeon standing upright on the cracked sidewalk, the small black Wayfarer sunglasses on its face, the small black pistol held in its right wing, the grey concrete wall, the curb, the litter, the cigarette butt, the white lane line, the passerby's legs in dark shorts and black clogs at the right edge. The pigeon is the only hero. The passerby simply finishes walking out of frame to the right.\n\nVIDEO PROMPT:\n0.0s to 2.0s: Open on the exact frame of @Image 1. The passerby's legs step out of frame right. The pigeon turns its head, then starts walking, upright on two feet with a slow, unbothered swagger, pistol still in its right wing hanging at its side, barrel down. It steps off the curb onto the asphalt. The phone camera drifts slightly and reframes late, a small bounce from the operator shifting weight.\n2.0s to 4.0s: The camera performs a shaky digital zoom in on the pigeon as it walks along the road toward the camera side of the street, slight focus hunt, the image gets a bit softer and noisier as the zoom tightens. Sunglasses stay on.\n4.0s to 6.0s: The camera pulls the zoom back a little and pans left, revealing the middle of the street ahead of the pigeon: a scruffy tabby street cat crouched on the asphalt with a real small grey mouse held in its mouth, and two more street cats, one black and one orange, sitting close on either side of it, all three looking down at the mouse. The pigeon keeps walking straight at them. Distant traffic passes in the background.\n6.0s to 8.5s: The pigeon stops about two meters from the cats, plants its feet, raises the pistol straight up over its head with its wing, pointed only at the empty sky, and fires two short blank shots upward, then a third. Small sharp muzzle flash, a puff of smoke, the wing kicks slightly with each recoil. The phone camera jolts hard with each crack, the operator flinches, the frame jumps and over-rotates, then corrects back onto the pigeon. Nothing and no one is hit.\n8.5s to 11.0s: All three cats startle at the first crack. The tabby drops the mouse. The cats bolt with real cat physics, low bodies, scrambling paws, tails puffed: the tabby sprints far down the road and shrinks into the distance, the black cat darts left under a parked car, the orange cat leaps sideways to the right and vanishes behind the curb. The freed mouse scurries fast across the asphalt and squeezes into a storm drain opening in the curb near the camera. The camera whips toward the fleeing cats, lags, then finds the pigeon again.\n11.0s to 15.0s: The pigeon lowers the pistol back to its side, barrel down, and continues its walk straight toward the camera across the road with the same slow gangster swagger, head bobbing, feet clicking on the asphalt. The camera performs a second shaky digital zoom in, slowly tightening on the pigeon's head and black sunglasses as it walks, focus breathing, sensor noise rising. The pigeon fills the lower frame, sunglasses on, pistol hanging at its side, and walks past the lens at the last moment. End on the pigeon close and slightly out of focus, camera still handheld and unsteady.\n\nAUDIO:\nNatural street ambience only: distant traffic hum, a car passing, wind on the phone microphone, the passerby's clogs slapping away, the pigeon's claws ticking on concrete then asphalt, <three short sharp pistol cracks echoing off the concrete wall, a fraction apart>, a muffled phone-mic clip and the operator's small startled breath on the first crack, cats hissing and yowling once, the scramble of paws on asphalt, a tiny mouse squeak and a scrape at the drain, then the ambience settles back to traffic and the pigeon's steady footsteps growing closer to the microphone. No music, no narration, no spoken words.\n\nCONSISTENCY:\nThe pigeon is the same bird from @Image 1 for the entire shot, identical feather markings and size. The black Wayfarer sunglasses stay on its face for the whole video and are never removed, never slip. The pistol never leaves its right wing. The pigeon stays upright on two feet, real pigeon anatomy, walks like a small person. The cats are real street cats, the mouse is a real small mouse. The location is the same street, same grey wall and curb, from the same across-the-street viewpoint. One continuous shot from one phone.\n\nNEGATIVE PROMPT: no cuts, no scene change, no smooth gimbal movement, no stabilization, no cinematic color grading, no cartoon, no CGI look, no plastic or toy look, no extra pigeons, no extra people in the foreground, no camera or phone visible, no drone, no sunglasses removed, no pistol dropped, no pistol pointed at any animal or person, no injuries, no blood, no cats hit, no mouse hurt, no floating objects, no teleporting cats, no morphing, no warping, no text, no captions, no watermark, no music, no narration.","imgs":["https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2103117707516542976/img/oscWiP5EWjeqPlys.jpg"]},{"i":19055,"text":"{\n  \"prompt_template_name\": \"Folk_Art_Hero_Product_Poster_BrandColor_Adaptive\",\n  \"instructions_for_generator\": \"User will provide only {BRAND_NAME}. Steps to follow: (1) Identify that brand's flagship/hero product. (2) Identify that brand's official brand color palette (primary logo color, secondary accent colors, and packaging colors as used in real-world branding). (3) Apply this exact folk-art poster illustration style and layout, but recolor every background shape, ornamental element, and packaging surface using ONLY colors derived from that brand's real identity — do not default to magenta/yellow/green unless those happen to be the brand's actual colors. (4) Select all decorative ingredient/thematic illustrations to be contextually relevant to that hero product's flavor, category, and use-case.\",\n\n  \"image_type\": \"Vertical poster-style product advertisement illustration\",\n  \"aspect_ratio\": \"4:5 portrait\",\n  \"art_style\": {\n    \"primary_style\": \"Mexican folk art / papel picado inspired flat illustration\",\n    \"rendering\": \"Textured flat vector illustration with visible grainy/paper texture overlay on all shapes\",\n    \"line_work\": \"Bold, thick, rounded outlines on every illustrated element, cartoon-poster style\",\n    \"shading\": \"Minimal cel-shading, soft highlight streaks, no realistic gradients\",\n    \"mood\": \"Vibrant, festive, celebratory, appetizing, culturally rich\"\n  },\n\n  \"brand_color_resolution\": {\n    \"step_1_primary_background_color\": \"Use the brand's dominant/primary logo color as the main background field color (the large arch/blob shape)\",\n    \"step_2_secondary_background_color\": \"Use the brand's secondary or complementary identity color for the surrounding corner fields\",\n    \"step_3_accent_colors\": \"Derive 2-3 accent colors for ornamental birds, florals, and flourishes by pulling from the brand's full identity system (packaging colors, secondary logo tones, or established brand gradient colors) — never invent unrelated colors\",\n    \"step_4_box_color\": \"Packaging box body color must match the brand's actual hero product packaging color scheme as closely as possible\",\n    \"step_5_contrast_check\": \"Ensure chosen palette maintains high contrast and poster vibrancy even if brand colors are naturally muted — deepen/saturate for illustration purposes only, do not shift hue\",\n    \"fallback_rule\": \"If brand has only one strong identity color, generate a harmonious festive palette using tints/shades/complements of that single color rather than introducing an unrelated color scheme\"\n  },\n\n  \"background\": {\n    \"base_layout\": \"Two-tone split background using brand primary and secondary colors as resolved above\",\n    \"top_and_side_corners_color\": \"Brand secondary identity color\",\n    \"main_field_shape\": \"Large arch or ornamental blob shape in brand primary identity color, emerging from bottom center, filling majority of frame\",\n    \"border_treatment\": \"Scalloped/dotted lace-like border along inner edge of the main shape, using brand secondary color dots against the primary color field, forming a perforated papel picado trim\"\n  },\n\n  \"framing_ornamental_elements\": {\n    \"top_center\": \"Small rounded badge/plaque shape at very top center in brand secondary color, reserved for a short promotional word or brand mark\",\n    \"top_center_motif\": \"Small stylized leaf/floral icon using brand accent colors above or inside the badge\",\n    \"upper_flanking_elements\": \"Two large symmetrical stylized folk-art birds (one left, one right), wings spread ornately, rendered using a gradient built from brand accent colors, facing inward toward the center product\",\n    \"mid_flanking_elements_left_right\": \"Symmetrical pairs of large decorative illustrations of ingredients/objects directly tied to the hero product's flavor or use, colored using brand accent palette where naturalistic color isn't essential to recognizability, positioned stacked vertically along both left and right sides\",\n    \"small_accent_squiggles\": \"Thin ribbon-like paint-splash or flourish squiggles in brand accent colors scattered near each flanking element for movement\",\n    \"lower_corner_bursts\": \"Two large layered floral/cloud-burst shapes in bottom left and right corners, made of overlapping petal forms using the full resolved brand accent palette\",\n    \"bottom_center_icon\": \"A small centered illustrated object symbolizing how the hero product is prepared or used traditionally, colored in brand primary/secondary tones, flanked by two small floral flourish splashes in accent colors\"\n  },\n\n  \"central_hero_element\": {\n    \"object\": \"Front-facing product packaging box of the brand's flagship/hero product, centered vertically and horizontally, slightly larger in height than width, standing upright\",\n    \"packaging_style\": \"Matches brand's real-world hero product packaging conventions and colorway, reinterpreted in this illustration's texture and line style\",\n    \"box_body_color\": \"Brand's actual hero product packaging base color, with darker shade of same hue for 3D box edge/side effect\",\n    \"box_border_decoration\": \"Thin ornamental scalloped ribbon trim in brand accent color running around the inner border of the front face, same style as outer background border\",\n    \"top_left_badge_on_box\": \"Small circular/rounded badge in contrasting brand accent color indicating quantity or unit count relevant to hero product\",\n    \"brand_logo_placement\": \"Bold brand wordmark logo centered in upper-middle of box front, rendered in the brand's actual logo colors and authentic typography style, on a ribbon/banner shape\",\n    \"tagline_under_logo\": \"Establishment date or brand heritage line in small caps directly under or above logo if authentic to brand\",\n    \"product_flavor_name\": \"Large bold rounded sans-serif headline text stating the specific hero product's flavor/variant name, white or brand-light text with brand-dark outline, arched or two-line stacked layout\",\n    \"central_circular_product_photo_window\": \"Large circular illustrated 'window' in the middle of the box showing a stylized top-down illustration of the actual hero product/food/result in use, with decorative petal/scalloped ring border in brand accent colors around the circle\",\n    \"surrounding_box_illustrations\": \"Small painterly illustrations of the product's real ingredients or components scattered around the circular window on the box face itself, colored naturalistically but harmonized with brand palette saturation level\",\n    \"lower_tagline\": \"Secondary marketing phrase in bold rounded text, two-line stacked, white/light with brand-dark outline, positioned below the circular window\",\n    \"bottom_box_footer_band\": \"Decorative striped or geometric pattern band near bottom of box using brand accent colors\",\n    \"bottom_box_fine_print\": \"Small white or light text at very bottom of box stating pack contents/specs, in a simple sans-serif\"\n  },\n\n  \"color_palette\": {\n    \"resolution_method\": \"100% derived from {BRAND_NAME}'s real identity system — primary logo color, secondary logo/packaging color, and 2-3 supporting accent colors pulled from official brand assets\",\n    \"overall_saturation\": \"high saturation, high contrast, poster-vibrant — brand colors may be deepened/intensified for illustration impact but hue must stay true to brand\",\n    \"no_generic_defaults\": \"Do not default to magenta/yellow/green unless independently verified as the resolved brand's actual colors\"\n  },\n\n  \"lighting_and_texture\": {\n    \"texture_overlay\": \"Subtle grain/noise texture across all flat color fields to mimic screen-printed or hand-painted poster look\",\n    \"lighting_style\": \"Flat frontal illustrated lighting, no realistic shadows except small drop shadow beneath central box for depth\",\n    \"highlight_style\": \"Painterly white/light streak highlights on rounded surfaces (fruits, birds, box edges)\"\n  },\n\n  \"composition_rules\": {\n    \"symmetry\": \"Strict vertical mirror symmetry on all background and flanking ornamental elements\",\n    \"focal_hierarchy\": \"Central product box is the clear largest, sharpest, most detailed focal point; background elements are supporting and slightly softer in detail\",\n    \"negative_space\": \"Background shapes fill nearly entire frame with minimal flat empty space, dense festive composition\"\n  },\n\n  \"exclusions\": [\n    \"no readable brand-external promotional badges or 'new product' callout text anywhere in the image\",\n    \"no extra text labels beyond the packaging's own brand name, flavor name, taglines, and contents line\",\n    \"no realistic photography, entire image must remain flat illustrated folk-art style\",\n    \"no unrelated ingredients that do not connect to the resolved hero product\",\n    \"no off-brand colors anywhere in background, ornamental elements, or packaging\"\n  ],\n\n  \"user_input_field\": {\n    \"BRAND_NAME\": \"{{user_provided_brand_name}}\"\n  }\n}","imgs":["https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HS_Jr4magAAs8vc.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HS_Jr4qaYAAbZwu.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HS_Jr4obUAArOhq.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HS_Jr4qa0AAXPkK.jpg"]},{"i":19056,"text":"Create a high-end independent art-book editorial poster using the uploaded photo as the EXACT visual reference.\n\nSTRICT FORMAT:\n- Vertical 3:4 canvas\n- Divide the composition horizontally into two equal 50/50 sections\n- Top half = original photograph\n- Bottom half = minimalist handmade-paper illustration\n\nTOP HALF — PHOTOGRAPH:\nPreserve the uploaded photograph faithfully and naturally.\nKeep the exact subject identity, facial features, pose, clothing, hairstyle, body position, objects, environment, composition, perspective, lighting and recognizable details.\nDo not redesign or replace the subject.\nDo not change the scene.\nApply only subtle premium editorial color grading with soft natural contrast, refined tones and realistic photographic texture.\nThe photograph should remain photographic and occupy exactly the entire top 50%.\n\nBOTTOM HALF — MINIMALIST ILLUSTRATION:\nReinterpret only the most recognizable elements from the original photo as a small centered handmade paper illustration.\n\nThe illustration must:\n- occupy only around 10–20% of the bottom section\n- remain clearly recognizable from the original photo\n- use delicate imperfect hand-drawn lines\n- use bold flat acrylic-like color shapes\n- have subtle handmade paper grain\n- have slightly organic imperfect edges\n- feel handcrafted rather than digitally perfect\n- use no more than 4 colors extracted from the original photograph\n- maintain generous warm off-white negative space around the illustration\n\nKeep the illustration small and understated.\nDo not let it dominate the bottom half.\n\nEDITORIAL DESIGN:\nCreate a quiet, poetic, refined independent art-book aesthetic.\nUse a warm off-white paper background in the bottom half.\nOptional: add extremely minimal editorial typography beneath the illustration using small elegant uppercase serif lettering with generous letter spacing.\nTypography must be subtle and secondary.\n\nVISUAL MOOD:\nquiet\npoetic\nminimal\nrefined\nartistic\npremium\nmuseum-catalogue / independent art-book aesthetic\nnatural\ntimeless\n\nSTRICTLY AVOID:\ncartoon style\nanime\nwatercolor\ncolored-pencil rendering\n3D rendering\nglossy effects\nphotorealistic illustration\nbusy composition\nlarge illustration\ncommercial advertising aesthetic\noversaturated colors\nheavy shadows\nexcessive typography\nextra objects\naltered identity\nchanged clothing\nchanged pose\nchanged facial features\n\nThe final image should look like a carefully designed contemporary art-book cover where the original photograph and its tiny handmade interpretation coexist in a restrained 50/50 editorial composition.","imgs":["https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HS_hFfpboAALBzG.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HS_hFfibUAAPBst.jpg"]},{"i":19057,"text":"请基于我上传的照片，生成一张独立的3:4竖版“玻璃错层”高级实验摄影作品。\n\n严格保持原始主体的身份、脸型、五官、发型、服装、姿态、产品结构、建筑关系、主体位置和原始场景不变。\n\n不要重新设计主体，不要换脸，不要换衣服，不要重新构图。\n\n首先分析原图中最值得被强调的视觉区域，例如：\n\n人物的眼睛、侧脸、嘴唇、手部、首饰、肩线；\n产品的瓶盖、金属边缘、玻璃瓶身、Logo附近；\n建筑的楼梯、立柱、窗线、空间纵深。\n\n然后在摄影机与主体之间真实放置3—5个透明光学介质。\n\n不要全部使用相同形状。\n\n根据画面内容组合使用：\n\n厚重透明水晶棱柱、\n切角光学玻璃块、\n长条透明玻璃板、\n不规则多面水晶、\n窄幅高透玻璃片。\n\n其中1—2块玻璃靠近镜头，形成明显的大尺度前景；\n其余玻璃位于中前景，以不同距离、厚度和角度分布。\n\n玻璃必须具有真实体积、厚度、边缘、切面、高光、反射和透视关系。\n\n让光线真正穿过玻璃，并产生真实光学现象：\n\n局部影像位置偏移，\n不同倍率的轻微放大与压缩，\n局部双像，\n边缘折射，\n少量光谱色散，\n高光分裂，\n镜面反射，\n前后空间叠层。\n\n不同玻璃的折射方向、倍率和位置不得完全一致。\n\n主体不能整体碎裂。\n\n至少保留50%—70%的主体清晰完整区域，第一眼必须能够准确识别人或产品；折射只发生在经过玻璃的局部区域。\n\n人物画面优先让玻璃切过：\n一只眼睛、半侧脸、嘴唇边缘、手部、肩线或首饰，\n不要同时破坏整张脸。\n\n产品画面优先让玻璃放大：\n瓶盖、金属件、透明材质、液体、切面或品牌结构。\n\n建筑画面优先利用玻璃重新切割：\n楼梯、立柱、窗户、天花线条和空间纵深。\n\n光线采用具有方向性的硬柔结合摄影光。\n\n可使用：\n侧逆光、\n顶部硬光、\n窄束聚光、\n夕阳斜光、\n珠宝棚拍高光。\n\n让玻璃边缘出现强烈但真实的高光，折射区域出现少量克制的彩色光谱，但禁止大面积彩虹。\n\n整体效果参考：\n高级时尚杂志实验摄影、\n珠宝广告摄影、\n香水商业大片、\n当代建筑编辑摄影。\n\n真实摄影质感，高对比但不过曝，细腻皮肤、真实金属、玻璃、水晶和织物材质，轻微胶片颗粒。\n\n最终效果必须像： 摄影师真的在镜头前架设了一组水晶与光学玻璃，通过真实折射一次拍摄完成， 而不是后期复制图层或数字故障效果。  \n\n禁止： 整张画面碎裂， 规则矩形复制， 赛博故障， 大量霓虹， 夸张彩虹， 人物复制， 多张完整人脸， 玻璃漂浮特效， 廉价万花筒， 镜像拼贴， 主体完全失焦， 塑料水晶， 明显AI特效感。","imgs":["https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HTBt9RMbsAAbhtO.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HTBt9RKbkAAfsoP.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HTBt9ROaMAIn9xF.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HTBt9RMawAAyuVn.jpg"]},{"i":19058,"text":"A sophisticated minimalist architectural art poster featuring [LANDMARK / STRUCTURE] as the central subject, illustrated in a refined hand-drawn architectural sketch style. Preserve the landmark’s recognizable silhouette, proportions, and defining architectural details, while transforming it into an elegant artistic composition.\n\nUse a limited monochromatic color palette inspired by the location, with soft vintage tones on a warm ivory/off-white paper background. Combine delicate ink lines, fine architectural hatching, subtle halftone texture, and lightly distressed print details.\n\nSurround the structure with a few abstract geometric shapes, soft translucent circles, subtle atmospheric elements, birds, or tiny contextual details that complement the landmark without overpowering it. Add a subtle sense of depth through overlapping layers and faded linework.\n\nInclude small minimalist typography on one side: [CITY / COUNTRY], [LANDMARK NAME], and optional coordinates or a short location descriptor, arranged like a premium travel-art print.\n\nClean negative space, editorial graphic design, museum-quality travel poster aesthetic, elegant composition, understated luxury, vintage screen-print texture, artistic architectural illustration, no people, no photorealistic background, no unnecessary objects, 4:5 vertical composition.\n\n[LANDMARK] reimagined as a collectible minimalist travel-art poster, combining architectural sketching, vintage printmaking, geometric abstract shapes, delicate linework, halftone texture, muted location-inspired colors, and elegant negative space. The landmark remains instantly recognizable but feels like a hand-crafted piece of modern graphic art. Add tiny birds, subtle environmental elements, coordinates, and minimal location typography. Premium editorial aesthetic, artistic, sophisticated, highly shareable, 4:5 vertical.","imgs":["https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HTCN9FZbkAAWNDr.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HTCN90ZasAAJ71X.jpg"]},{"i":19059,"text":"Create a sophisticated minimalist editorial art poster featuring [PERSON / LANDMARK / STRUCTURE] as the central subject, inspired by premium travel photography and refined hand-drawn illustration.\n\nPreserve the subject’s recognizable identity, proportions, silhouette, defining details, and visual character. Combine realistic elements with elegant artistic interpretation.\n\nUse a warm ivory paper background with a limited vintage color palette inspired by the subject’s location or personality. Add delicate ink outlines, architectural sketch lines, subtle hatching, halftone texture, faded print effects, and soft watercolor-like washes.\n\nCreate a sense of visual storytelling by incorporating subtle surrounding elements connected to the subject — such as [CITY / COUNTRY / CULTURE / PROFESSION / LANDMARK DETAILS / NATURE] — while maintaining generous negative space and a clean luxury-editorial composition.\n\nAdd small, tasteful typography:\n[NAME / LANDMARK]\n[CITY / COUNTRY]\n[SHORT DESCRIPTOR / YEAR / COORDINATES]\n\nStyle: museum-quality travel poster, contemporary editorial illustration, vintage printmaking, refined hand-drawn detail, understated luxury, sophisticated composition.\n\nNo unnecessary objects, no clutter, no distorted features, no exaggerated proportions, no generic stock-art appearance.\n\nFormat: 4:5 vertical, high-resolution, premium collectible poster aesthetic.\n\n[SUBJECT] reimagined as a timeless visual story.","imgs":["https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HTDy61rawAANZna.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HTDy61taYAA3MJk.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HTDy6-IaQAAHk_1.jpg"]},{"i":19060,"text":"Create a sophisticated 3:4 vertical editorial art poster with GPT Image 2.5, using the uploaded photograph as the primary visual reference.\n\nDivide the composition into two perfectly balanced horizontal halves.\n\nUpper 50% — Original Photograph\nKeep the uploaded image almost completely untouched. Preserve the exact identity, facial features, pose, styling, clothing, objects, composition, lighting, colors, proportions, and natural photographic texture. The image should still look like the original photograph, enhanced only with subtle high-end editorial color grading.\n\nLower 50% — Artistic Interpretation\nTransform the key visual elements of the photograph into a tiny, centered handmade-paper artwork. Reduce the scene into a few recognizable shapes and imperfect hand-drawn lines, as if created for an independent contemporary art publication.\n\nUse:\n\n- warm off-white handmade paper\n- delicate imperfect ink-like outlines\n- simple flat acrylic-inspired shapes\n- organic uneven edges\n- subtle natural paper fibers and grain\n- maximum 4 colors sampled from the original photograph\n\nThe miniature artwork should occupy only 10–20% of the lower half, leaving most of the space intentionally empty. Keep it understated and poetic rather than detailed.\n\nAdd optional tiny editorial typography only if it naturally complements the composition. Typography should be minimal, elegant, and secondary to the artwork.\n\nVisual direction: contemporary art book, quiet luxury, gallery editorial, handmade print, refined minimalism, poetic negative space, sophisticated composition.\n\nDo not make it: cartoonish, childish, watercolor, colored-pencil, 3D, glossy, overly digital, highly detailed, colorful, busy, or commercial-looking.\n\nThe final result should feel like a limited-edition independent art-book cover where a real photograph and its handmade artistic memory coexist in one composition.","imgs":["https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HTD3x-TbsAEEUHz.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HTD3ynUbUAA0zkc.jpg"]},{"i":19061,"text":"上传图1、图2、图3、图4，生成一张独立的3:4竖版写实时尚摄影作品。\n请严格按照以下职责使用参考图：\n图1：人物身份参考\n只参考脸型、五官、发型、肤色、年龄与体型。最终人物必须保持图1的身份，不继承图1的服装、姿势和背景。\n图2：服装造型参考\n只参考服装的版型、颜色、面料、纹理、配饰与穿着层次。将整套服装准确穿在图1人物身上，不使用图2人物的脸、发型和身体特征。\n图3：姿势与构图参考\n只参考身体朝向、手臂位置、腿部重心、视线方向、景别与人物在画面中的位置。不继承图3的人物身份、服装和场景。\n图4：场景与光线参考\n只参考空间结构、环境材质、主光方向、色温、阴影关系与整体氛围。不复制图4中原有的人物、文字和标志。\n最终画面必须呈现为一次真实拍摄：\n图1的人物，穿着图2的服装，完成图3的姿势，真实站在图4的环境中。\n统一人物与场景的透视、光线、色温和接触阴影。服装自然贴合身体，保留真实褶皱与材质反光；双脚稳定接触地面，手指结构完整，人物边缘不存在拼贴感。\n禁止混合人物身份、借用错误服装、改变服装颜色、复制参考图文字、增加无关配饰、肢体变形、悬浮脚、错误阴影和四张图片拼贴。\n💡 核心逻辑\n四张参考图不能拥有相同的话语权。\n人物图负责“是谁”，服装图负责“穿什么”，姿势图负责“怎么站”，场景图负责“在哪里”。\n每张图只完成一项任务，AI才不会把参考内容互相串用。\n\n📌 一句话总结\n不要让AI猜四张图该怎么用，直接规定：谁负责脸，谁负责衣服，谁负责动作，谁负责整个世界。","imgs":["https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HTG-ebiagAAsBST.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HTG-ebrbwAA43Fh.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HTG-ebfaUAAmGWO.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HTG-ebhbMAAaNzK.jpg"]},{"i":19062,"text":"Create a breathtaking, surreal editorial artwork based on [PERSON / LANDMARK / OBJECT / CITY], built around the concept “THE WORLD INSIDE A SHADOW.”\n\nShow the main subject as a refined, almost museum-quality object or scene against a vast warm ivory paper background. The subject casts an unusually long, sharply defined shadow.\n\nBut instead of being empty, the shadow contains an entire hidden world connected to the subject.\n\nInside the shadow, reveal miniature scenes, architecture, landscapes, people, streets, memories, symbols, objects, and cultural details associated with [PERSON / LANDMARK / CITY / COUNTRY]. The shadow should feel like a secret parallel universe — as if the true story of the subject exists inside its silhouette.\n\nThe actual subject remains elegant, minimal, realistic and recognizable, while the shadow becomes increasingly detailed, surreal and dreamlike toward its farthest edge.\n\nCreate a seamless transition from realistic materials into delicate hand-drawn ink, architectural linework, tiny paper-cut elements, vintage engraving textures, subtle halftone dots and miniature painted details.\n\nUse extreme visual storytelling and micro-details that reward close inspection.\n\nComposition:\n\nsophisticated editorial art direction\nstrong central silhouette\nenormous flowing shadow extending diagonally across the canvas\ngenerous negative space\nvisual hierarchy from simple subject → complex hidden world\nno unnecessary objects\nno clutter\n\nMaterial language:\nfine art paper, ink, graphite, engraved textures, subtle embossing, handmade print imperfections, delicate paper fibers, restrained collage elements.\n\nColor palette:\nwarm ivory, charcoal, faded black, muted stone, dusty beige, with one controlled signature color inspired by [COUNTRY / CITY / SUBJECT].\n\nLighting:\nsoft museum lighting, subtle natural shadow, cinematic but understated.\n\nMood:\nmysterious, intelligent, poetic, luxurious, slightly surreal, timeless.\n\nAdd extremely minimal typography:\n[NAME]\nsmall refined serif type placed away from the artwork, like a museum exhibition label.\n\nNo generic fantasy aesthetic, no excessive glow, no neon, no random decorative objects, no cheesy symbolism, no overcrowding.\n\n4:5 vertical — premium contemporary art poster — museum exhibition quality — surreal editorial photography fused with handcrafted fine art — ultra-detailed — sophisticated and original.","imgs":["https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HTHR5y0bQAAu1K6.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HTHR5yya4AASS9N.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HTHR5ysaoAAnX2j.jpg"]},{"i":19063,"text":"Create a short cinematic, humorous lifestyle video about a young woman who refuses to sleep because she finally has time for herself after work.\nScene 1 — After Work\nLate evening. A tired young woman arrives home after a long workday, drops her bag, changes into comfortable clothes and finally collapses onto her bed. Warm, cozy bedroom lighting. She looks exhausted but relieved.\nScene 2 — “Finally, Me Time”\nShe picks up her phone and smiles. The room becomes darker and quieter while the phone screen illuminates her face. She scrolls through videos, messages, memes and social media.\nAdd subtle on-screen text:\n“Me: I should sleep early tonight.”\nShe checks the time: 11:47 PM.\nShe shrugs and keeps scrolling.\nScene 3 — The Time Thief\nTime passes rapidly through a cinematic time-lapse.\n11:47 PM → 12:38 AM → 1:52 AM → 3:07 AM\nWith every time jump, make her eyes slightly more tired and the dark circles underneath them progressively darker.\nThe phone remains perfectly bright and addictive.\nOn-screen text:\n“But I didn’t get enough ME TIME today.”\nScene 4 — Visual Metaphor\nMake the concept surreal and funny: the phone slowly grows larger while she becomes smaller, as if the phone is consuming the night.\nHer dark circles become exaggerated like soft ink shadows beneath her eyes.\nShe looks at herself in the mirror.\nShe is exhausted, hair slightly messy, huge dark circles under her eyes.\nShe looks at the phone.\nThen back at herself.\nThen immediately unlocks the phone again.\nScene 5 — The Punchline\nClose-up of her face glowing from the phone at 3:47 AM.\nShe whispers:\n“Tomorrow I’ll fix my sleep schedule.”\nCut to black.\nText appears:\n“Tomorrow’s problem.”\nTiny final text:\n“Me time: 4 hours\nSleep: 3 hours\nRegrets: loading…”\nStyle: cinematic realistic lifestyle film, relatable internet humor, warm bedroom lighting mixed with cool phone light, subtle exaggerated dark circles, expressive facial acting, smooth camera movements, realistic skin and fabric, shallow depth of field, natural handheld moments, tasteful comedy, premium social-media reel aesthetic, 9:16 vertical, 15–20 seconds, seamless time transitions, highly polished visual storytelling.\nExtra visual trick: make the dark circles progressively resemble a clock shadow under her eyes. It makes the joke more visually unique instead of just showing someone looking tired.","imgs":["https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2103770434743480320/img/XahcBmxA96pFNef_.jpg"]},{"i":19064,"text":"控制对于复杂的空间运动有很大的瑕疵，人物站哪、车从哪冲出来、镜头怎么移动……这些全交给AI猜，结果就是越重抽越乱。\n今天这个词叫「灰盒预演」：先用方块、圆柱、低模人物把空间和运镜搭出来，再让AI负责角色、材质与风格。\n我用MiniMax Design协作我生成了附件这个效果，它可以调用Blender协助建模，而如果没有Blender也没关系，简单3D场景、线框草图，甚至几张标出运动路径的草图都能用。\n\n🎯 核心提示词：\n以图1的灰盒预演为唯一镜头与动作参考，生成一段10秒、9:16的电影感视频。\n严格保留原参考中的：\n- 摄像机位置、焦段感与运动路径\n- 人物和道具的位置、比例及朝向\n- 每个动作发生的顺序与时间节点\n- 前景、中景、背景的空间关系\n- 遮挡、进出画和镜头停顿\n将灰盒中的占位模型替换为完整角色、车辆、建筑和环境，角色身份参考图2，整体美术风格参考图3。\n先准确还原空间与镜头，再增加材质、光影、粒子和环境细节。动作连贯，速度自然，空间关系稳定。\n不要改变构图，不要重新设计运镜，不要让人物瞬移，不要交换动作顺序，不要擅自增加环绕镜头，不要生成重复角色或漂移物体。\n\n🔁 延伸玩法：\n- 追车戏：先用方块确定两辆车的距离和超车路线\n- 打斗戏：先用低模人物排好攻击、闪避和倒地节奏\n- 产品广告：先确定产品旋转、镜头推进和灯光切换\n- 一镜到底：先把完整路径跑通，再统一角色与场景风格\n- 多镜头短片：把每个灰盒镜头连成预演，再逐镜精修\n\n⚙️ 关键控制点：\n1. 灰盒越简单越好，只解决位置、时间与镜头\n2. 先检查动作是否读得懂，再添加风格参考\n3. 复杂镜头拆成3—5秒一段，成功率更高\n4. 灰盒是结构参考，角色图负责身份，风格图负责质感，三者不要混用\n5. 生成后优先修空间错误，最后才修服装、纹理和光效\n\n📌 一句话总结：\n灰盒预演，不是先把画面做漂亮，而是先把镜头想明白——让AI负责完成，而不是负责猜。","imgs":["https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HTMcvUXacAAtqhm.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HTMc0R6bUAAm5s6.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HTMc0R7aAAA1Bdc.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2104056955149193216/img/QQzZD1zbvX8c_T9A.jpg"]},{"i":19065,"text":"Create an exceptionally original minimalist architectural art poster featuring [LANDMARK].\n\nDo NOT directly draw, paint, or fill the landmark.\n\nInstead, create the landmark entirely through negative space.\n\nThe central silhouette of [LANDMARK] remains almost completely untouched — warm ivory paper showing through naturally. Around this empty silhouette, extremely delicate graphite lines describe the world that surrounds it: architectural measurements, tiny streets, distant rooftops, clouds, birds, shadows, perspective guides, fragments of maps and subtle environmental contours.\n\nThe surrounding drawing becomes denser near the edges of the landmark, making the untouched negative space gradually reveal the unmistakable silhouette of [LANDMARK].\n\nSome construction lines intentionally continue through the empty silhouette but become extremely faint, as if the artist started drawing the landmark and then erased it.\n\nAdd one unexpected detail: a single continuous pencil line travels around the landmark without ever drawing its actual outline. At one point, the line breaks and leaves a tiny handwritten coordinate or date.\n\nUse warm ivory paper, graphite pencil, extremely fine architectural linework, subtle eraser dust, paper fibers, faint halftone imperfections and soft natural shadows.\n\nColor palette: almost entirely monochrome graphite and ivory, with one extremely subtle accent inspired by [CITY/COUNTRY].\n\nSmall refined typography placed in generous negative space:\n\n[LANDMARK NAME]\n[CITY, COUNTRY]\n\n“drawn by everything around it.”\n\nThe composition must feel mysterious, intelligent and unexpectedly beautiful — like a contemporary museum artwork rather than a conventional travel poster.\n\nNo photorealistic background. No obvious illustration of the landmark. No decorative clutter. No excessive typography. No people.\n\n4:5 vertical, ultra-minimal, sophisticated editorial design, tactile handmade paper, elegant negative space, precise architectural details, smooth visual flow, premium contemporary gallery aesthetic.","imgs":["https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HTNlkQXa4AAcM6G.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HTNlkQVbkAAY9A6.jpg"]},{"i":19066,"text":"（欢迎返图）：\n摄影风格：日间清亮高光CCD生活照风\n写真方向：都市互动时尚写真\n场景方向：现代数字艺术水幕区 / 白色互动屏幕 / 细线水幕 / 浅灰平台 / 极简城市建筑\n服装方向：覆盆子粉色修身Polo短款上衣 + 冷白色低腰A字超短裙\n气质标签：甜酷、明亮、时尚、俏皮、夏日感\n五官方向：高级元气初恋脸\n身形方向：轻盈纤细\n线条强调：强\n镜头方向：大腿及上半身\n姿态动作：从细线水幕边缘经过，一只手轻拨头发，身体正面略偏侧，回头看镜头\n光线氛围：晴天高亮自然光 + 白色互动屏幕形成大面积柔亮补光 + 水幕形成少量高光点\n滤镜效果：高亮清晰粉白CCD色彩 + 鲜明中间调 + 白净肤色 + 轻颗粒 + 极轻数码锐度\n画幅比例：9:16\n补充要求：水幕只能做少量高光点，不能雾化整图；覆盆子粉显色饱和但不荧光；短款上衣露出腰腹和肚脐，胸线清楚但自然，画面整体明亮通透","imgs":["https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HTnmb2YbUAEI896.jpg"]},{"i":19067,"text":"A 2:3 vertical-format image depicting a sci-fi scene that mimics authentic high-altitude snow mountain expedition photography. A spherical survey machine, towering dozens of stories high, stands atop a narrow snow ridge; its massive, silvery-white spherical shell dominates the upper frame, featuring a deep-black optical aperture composed of concentric circles—with lens layers receding into darkness and only a tiny white reflection at the center, resembling a giant eye silently watching humanity without emitting any beams. The shell displays intricate armored plating, scattered circular vents, slender antennas, and maintenance ports, marked only by the black text \"GenVizu\" with no other characters or numbers. Beneath the shell lies a heavy, exposed black framework comprising cooling systems, hydraulic structures, and two sets of colossal tank treads that grip the snow along the ridge, conveying a distinct sense of massive weight. The white shell shows patches of frost and slight weathering, with snow accumulated in the black crevices; wind whips up fine snow from the right, yet the machinery remains clearly visible rather than obscured by heavy fog. In the foreground, two adult explorers clad in dark high-altitude protective gear and carrying equipment packs walk away from the camera toward the machine, holding trekking poles and small scanners; each figure occupies less than one-tenth of the frame's height, moving cautiously and leaving footprints along the ridge that emphasize their smallness and vulnerability. Distant mountains fade into the pale atmosphere, with a tiny drone serving merely as a scale reference. The image features low-saturation cool gray-white tones, realistic diffused sunlight, natural deep shadows, credible lens perspective, and fine snow-surface textures, evoking a documentary-style atmosphere of the unknown, silence, and oppressive scale. There is no combat, no heroic posing, and no extraneous text, watermarks, concept-art stylization, or artificial \"plastic\" rendering.","imgs":["https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HTN8V_QbIAA9rOH.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HTN8V_Va4AABJ1F.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HTN8V_RbwAAesYG.jpg"]},{"i":19068,"text":"TOTAL DURATION: 30 SECONDS\nSTYLE: Ultra-realistic Hollywood thriller, photorealistic cinematography, natural performances, realistic physics, cinematic lighting, restrained suspense, premium production design, 35mm anamorphic look, subtle film grain, realistic depth of field.\n\n0–4 SEC — THE WARNING\n\nNight. Heavy rain hits the windows of a secluded modern house. A dim hallway stretches into darkness. The young woman slowly enters the frame, immediately sensing that something is wrong.\n\nCamera: Slow handheld tracking shot behind her, subtle natural camera movement.\nAudio: Rain, distant thunder, quiet breathing, faint house creaks.\nMood: Uneasy silence and anticipation.\n\n4–8 SEC — SOMETHING MOVES\n\nShe stops. A faint movement appears at the far end of the living room. She slowly turns her head.\n\nLightning briefly illuminates the room, revealing several intruders partially concealed in the shadows.\n\nCamera: Slow push-in toward her face, then rack focus from her eyes toward the silhouettes.\nPerformance: Controlled fear, widened eyes, shallow breathing.\nAudio: Thunder suddenly rolls closer, followed by complete silence.\n\n8–13 SEC — THE REALIZATION\n\nThe woman remains completely still. One intruder subtly shifts position.\n\nHer eyes move toward a shotgun lying on a nearby table.\n\nCamera: Extreme close-up of her eyes → cut to the shotgun → cut back to her face.\nLighting: A cold lightning flash briefly outlines the weapon and the surrounding darkness.\nAudio: Her breathing becomes slightly louder; faint heartbeat-like bass begins.\n\n13–19 SEC — THE WALK\n\nShe slowly begins walking toward the table.\n\nEvery footstep echoes through the quiet room. The intruders remain motionless, watching her.\n\nCamera: Low-angle tracking shot beside her legs → slow side profile → close-up of her hand approaching the table.\nPerformance: Fear controlled by determination; no exaggerated movements.\n\n19–23 SEC — THE GRAB\n\nHer hand suddenly closes around the shotgun.\n\nShe pauses for one tense second.\n\nThe room becomes completely silent.\n\nCamera: Extreme close-up of her hand gripping the weapon → rapid rack focus to the intruders.\nLighting: Lightning flashes across the room, revealing everyone's faces for a split second.\n\n23–27 SEC — THE TURN\n\nShe slowly turns around and faces the intruders.\n\nThe camera moves around her shoulder, revealing the silhouettes ahead.\n\nNobody speaks.\n\nCamera: Slow 180-degree cinematic arc, ending in a dramatic frontal shot.\nPerformance: Her expression changes from fear to controlled determination.\n\n27–30 SEC — THE STANDOFF\n\nWide shot.\n\nShe stands alone in the center of the room, shotgun held defensively, while the intruders remain spread across the darkness.\n\nA final lightning flash freezes the composition.\n\nCamera: Extremely slow push-in toward her face.\n\nAudio: Thunder crack → silence → single deep cinematic impact.\n\nEND ON: Her unwavering expression as the screen cuts to black.\n\nVISUAL QUALITY: Photorealistic skin, realistic hair movement, physically accurate shadows, detailed environments, natural cloth simulation, realistic rain and reflections, cinematic volumetric lighting, subtle lens imperfections, anamorphic bokeh, HDR, restrained color grading, authentic Hollywood thriller cinematography.\n\nIMPORTANT: No gore, no graphic violence, no exaggerated action. The suspense must come from silence, pacing, acting, framing, lighting, sound, and anticipation.","imgs":["https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2104190858824482816/img/L9Qv-L5w6WKZ3772.jpg"]},{"i":19069,"text":"A fine-art studio portrait with dramatic butterfly lighting and realistic skin texture.\n\nPortrait Series - Part 3\n\nPrompt:\n\n{\n  \"style_prompt_template\": {\n    \"subject\": \"{{PERSON_NAME_OR_IMAGE}}\",\n    \"aspect_ratio\": \"9:16 vertical\",\n    \"canvas_size_guidance\": \"1080x1920 or equivalent 9:16\",\n    \"shot_type\": \"medium portrait shot, zoomed out 50% from tight close-up, head-to-mid-torso visible, facing camera\",\n    \"photography_style\": \"dramatic black and white studio portrait, editorial/fine-art photography\",\n    \"composition\": {\n      \"face_position\": \"subject's face centered both horizontally and vertically in the frame\",\n      \"face_size_in_frame\": \"face occupies roughly 20-25% of frame height, not tightly cropped, ample negative space around subject\",\n      \"eye_line\": \"eyes aligned at approximate vertical center of the canvas\",\n      \"headroom\": \"generous margin above the hair, clear dark space visible above head\",\n      \"crop\": \"visible down to mid-chest or waist, more of the suit and shoulders shown, wider view than a tight headshot\",\n      \"surrounding_space\": \"large area of negative black space surrounding subject on left, right, top, and bottom\",\n      \"alignment\": \"subject facing straight into camera, symmetrical framing, no off-center offset\"\n    },\n    \"lighting\": {\n      \"type\": \"single hard top-down spotlight (butterfly/Paramount lighting)\",\n      \"quality\": \"harsh, narrow beam creating strong falloff\",\n      \"key_highlight\": \"top of hair and forehead catch bright rim light\",\n      \"shadow_behavior\": \"deep shadows under brow, cheekbones, and jawline; steep light-to-dark gradient across face\",\n      \"background_light\": \"none; background falls into near-total darkness with faint gradient near top edge, spotlight cone visible in wider frame\"\n    },\n    \"color_treatment\": \"monochrome black and white, high contrast, deep blacks, no gray midtone flatness\",\n    \"background\": \"solid black or near-black, subtle vignette, no visible texture or props, large expanse of negative space\",\n    \"wardrobe\": \"dark tailored suit jacket, white dress shirt, dark tie, formal/business attire, full torso visible\",\n    \"expression_and_pose\": \"neutral to serious expression, calm and composed, minimal smile, direct gaze into lens, relaxed shoulders\",\n    \"skin_and_texture_detail\": \"visible natural skin texture, pores, fine wrinkles, stubble if present, unretouched realism\",\n    \"hair_detail\": \"individual strands visible and crisply lit, natural texture, not overly styled\",\n    \"camera_and_lens\": \"shot as if on medium format camera, 50mm-85mm equivalent lens, greater working distance from subject, shallow depth of field, tack-sharp focus on eyes\",\n    \"grain_and_finish\": \"fine film-like grain, high dynamic range, crisp micro-contrast, glossy editorial finish\",\n    \"mood\": \"intense, powerful, cinematic, timeless\"\n  },\n  \"negative_prompt\": \"color cast, flat lighting, soft focus, blown highlights on face, busy background, smiling broadly, low contrast, blurry details, off-center face, face cropped at edge, horizontal framing, extreme close-up, tight crop, face filling entire frame\"\n}","imgs":["https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HT2loJAaUAAGoO2.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HT2loJFagAAI5ZF.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HT2loI_aEAAe99q.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HT2loJCbIAA0ZHY.jpg"]},{"i":19070,"text":"请基于我上传的照片，制作一张独立的 3:4竖版「凸镜鱼眼双生」海报，画面上下严格 1:1分割。\n\n上半：完整保留原始照片，仅轻微统一调色。\n\n下半：严格保持 同一人物、同一张脸、同一服装、同一动作、同一地点和主体身份，将同一场景重构为真实 8mm极端鱼眼 / 圆形凸面镜摄影。\n\n要求：\n\n主体位于画面中心\n\n人脸保持准确，不拉坏五官\n\n建筑、道路、天空和环境向边缘自然弯曲\n\n越靠近边缘，球面透视越明显\n\n保留真实镜面高光、边缘暗角和空间畸变\n\n整体像真实鱼眼镜头拍摄，不是液化特效\n\n**禁止：**换脸、换衣、换地点、复制人物、拉坏身体、随机扭曲物体、超现实融化、明显AI感。\n\n🔁延伸玩法\n\n人物街拍\n最适合街道、商场、地铁口。\n人物不变，整个城市向四周弯开。\n\n旅行照片\n建筑、教堂、广场、城市地标都很好用。\n特别适合本身就有大量线条的场景。\n\n汽车照片\n车身保持完整，周围道路和建筑形成夸张球面透视。\n宠物照片\n宠物放在画面中心，环境拉开，会有很强的趣味感。\n产品照片\n鞋、相机、饮料、潮玩放在中心，周围环境做极端鱼眼，很适合潮流广告。\n\n⚙️参数技巧\n1. 主体尽量放中间\n鱼眼最怕脸在边缘。\n\n人物越靠近中心，五官越稳定。\n2. 要写真实镜头，不要只写“弯曲”\n\n建议加入：\n8mm fisheye lens\n\nspherical distortion\nconvex mirror\n\nextreme wide angle\n\ncircular perspective\n\n3. 背景线条越多越出效果\n\n街道、建筑、栏杆、天花板、地砖，都特别适合。\n\n4. 别把人物也一起拉坏\n\n核心控制：\n\n主体身份锁定，环境产生鱼眼畸变。\n\n5. 想更夸张可以做圆形凸镜版\n\n直接让整个画面出现在交通凸面镜、商场镜面或金属反射球里，视觉冲击会更强。\n\n📌一句话总结\n\n上传一张普通照片，让AI不换人、不换地方，只把整个世界拍弯。","imgs":["https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HTRAfT0bwAAHkMx.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HTRAfT0awAAzyRg.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HTRApQqbEAAXCna.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HTRApQpaQAA7L7L.jpg"]},{"i":19071,"text":"国庆节，无论是给自己出片，还是给女朋友/老婆出片，都无敌了！\n\n提示词如下👇：\n\n请像一位美学/美容顾问一样，从我附带的照片中分析我的外貌。\n\n识别出能让我看起来更精致和谐的最高影响力的变化，包括发型/发式/发色、眉毛、眼妆、皮肤/妆容位置、嘴唇，以及整体面部平衡。\n\n请针对我的实际特征给出具体建议，而不是泛泛而谈。  然后，生成这张确切照片的现实“之后”版本，展示你推荐的焕然一新效果。保持我可辨识为同一个人，并保留我的面部解剖结构，除非你特别推荐细微的结构调整。\n\n尽可能保持相同的姿势、相机角度、表情、光线、服装和背景。  让这些变化精致且现实，而不是夸张的美颜滤镜。优先考虑高影响力、低风险的造型调整。\n\n不要自动让我脸变瘦、鼻子变小、嘴唇变大、眼睛变大，或皮肤不切实际地完美。  对于头发，选择最能衬托我个人比例的发型、发色、分线、蓬松度和面部框架。\n\n对于妆容，优化眉形、眼线/睫毛、腮红/轮廓位置、唇部定义和肤色，同时保持自然。  \n\n生成一张前后对比照片，带有照片标注，解释每项变化，类似于专业美容咨询。","imgs":["https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HTRh2nvbAAAIdMr.jpg"]},{"i":19072,"text":"Create an exceptionally original minimalist architectural art poster featuring [LANDMARK] in [CITY, COUNTRY].\n\nDepict the landmark in its recognizable natural architectural appearance, with its authentic proportions, distinctive structure, materials, and characteristic details. Combine fine graphite architectural drawing with subtle vintage watercolor washes, creating the feeling of a sophisticated illustrated travel archive.\n\nThe landmark should be the central visual focus, surrounded by an intricate but restrained world of extremely delicate architectural linework: construction measurements, perspective guides, tiny streets, rooftops, surrounding buildings, local landscape, clouds, birds, shadows, fragments of maps, compass marks, elevation studies, structural details, and subtle environmental contours.\n\nUse a layered visual language where some elements are highly detailed while others fade into the paper, creating depth without making the composition feel crowded.\n\nAdd one unexpected artistic detail: a single continuous pencil line travels around the landmark without directly tracing its outline. Allow it to occasionally intersect with construction lines, then break at one point beside a tiny handwritten coordinate, date, measurement, or architectural note.\n\nUse warm ivory handmade paper, graphite pencil, extremely fine ink lines, delicate watercolor washes, subtle eraser dust, visible paper fibers, faint halftone imperfections, soft natural shadows, and lightly weathered archival texture.\n\nColor palette\n\nKeep the overall artwork muted, sophisticated, and vintage. Use warm ivory and graphite as the foundation, with the landmark shown in its authentic recognizable colors through restrained watercolor washes.\n\nAdd one subtle accent color inspired by [CITY/COUNTRY] — for example:\n\n- Italy → muted terracotta\n- Japan → restrained vermilion\n- France → faded blue\n- UK → muted navy or burgundy\n- India → subtle saffron\n- USA → muted teal or dusty red\n\nAvoid bright digital colors.\n\nSurrounding details\n\nInclude carefully chosen elements associated with [CITY/COUNTRY], such as:\n\n- local architecture\n- landscape or geography\n- streets and rooftops\n- transportation\n- vegetation\n- small cultural details\n- map fragments\n- architectural ornaments\n- elevation or measurement diagrams\n- compass rose\n- coordinates\n- faint historical annotations\n\nThese details should frame and contextualize the landmark rather than compete with it.\n\nTypography\n\nPlace small, refined typography in generous negative space:\n\n[LANDMARK NAME]\n[CITY, COUNTRY]\n\n“drawn by everything around it.”\n\nUse elegant editorial serif typography with generous spacing. Add only a few tiny handwritten architectural annotations or coordinates.\n\nArtistic direction\n\nThe final composition should feel mysterious, intelligent, timeless, and unexpectedly beautiful — somewhere between a vintage European travel poster, an architect's working sketch, a museum exhibition print, and a collector's archival illustration.\n\nNo people.\nNo photorealistic background.\nNo excessive typography.\nNo decorative clutter.\nNo neon colors.\nNo glossy digital rendering.\nNo cartoon aesthetic.\nNo generic stock-travel-poster appearance.\n\n4:5 vertical composition, premium editorial design, tactile handmade paper, sophisticated architectural illustration, precise fine-line details, subtle watercolor, elegant negative space, balanced visual hierarchy, museum-quality contemporary art poster.","imgs":["https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HTRlfFibYAA3Fed.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HTRlfFoaIAAWuqi.jpg"]},{"i":19073,"text":"Using the supplied first frame as the exact opening image, generate a 30-second horizontal 4:3 photorealistic lifestyle influencer vlog.\n\nVIDEO CONCEPT\n\nA realistic “Day in My Life” vlog following Mara through a relaxed sunny day in New York City:\n\n1. Morning introduction at home\n2. Quick green smoothie in the kitchen\n3. Getting dressed to leave\n4. Walking through the city\n5. Browsing a clothing store\n6. Meeting Elise at a café\n7. Walking and relaxing together in a sunny park\n8. Casual selfie sign-off\n\nThe video must feel spontaneous and personal, combining front-facing smartphone selfies, handheld point-of-view details and a few believable third-person shots recorded by a friend.\n\nIDENTITY CONTINUITY\n\nMara must preserve:\n- Same face\n- Same hazel-green eyes\n- Same freckles\n- Same long chestnut hair\n- Same body proportions\n- Same grey T-shirt\n- Same jeans\n- Same jewelry\n\nShe adds the black leather jacket, sneakers and tan shoulder bag before leaving the apartment. They must not appear before she physically puts them on.\n\nElise appears only during the café and park scenes.\n\nNo identity changes, face replacement or spontaneous outfit transformation.\n\nCAMERA RULES\n\nUse three clearly motivated camera perspectives:\n\n1. Mara’s front-facing handheld smartphone camera\n2. Mara’s rear-camera point-of-view detail shots\n3. Short third-person shots filmed by Elise or made with a phone placed on a stable surface\n\nEvery camera change must have a logical reason.\n\nTransitions should use:\n- Mara’s palm briefly covering the lens\n- Refrigerator door passing across the camera\n- Jacket fabric crossing the frame\n- A yellow taxi or pedestrian passing close to the lens\n- Shopping bag passing across the camera\n- A controlled whip pan following Mara’s movement\n\nDo not teleport between locations without a visible transition.\n\n0.0–3.5 SECONDS — MORNING SELFIE INTRODUCTION\n\nContinue directly from the first frame.\n\nMara holds the phone at arm’s length and says naturally:\n\n“Good morning. I thought I’d bring you along today.”\n\nShe smiles, shifts her weight and brushes one strand of hair away from her face.\n\nThe camera moves slightly with her breathing and wrist position.\nHer eyes look primarily into the lens, occasionally checking the phone screen.\n\nShe begins walking toward the kitchen while keeping the selfie camera on herself.\n\n3.5–6.5 SECONDS — KITCHEN SMOOTHIE\n\nMara turns the camera toward a bright compact kitchen.\n\nUse three quick but coherent shots:\n- Hand placing spinach, banana and frozen mango into a blender\n- Close-up of pale green smoothie pouring into one transparent glass\n- Selfie shot of Mara raising the finished drink beside her face\n\nThe kitchen has:\n- White cabinets\n- Pale stone counter\n- Stainless-steel faucet\n- Bowl of fruit\n- Bright window light\n- Ordinary small appliances\n\nMara takes one real sip, swallows and gives a small approving nod.\n\nShe says:\n\n“Quick breakfast, then I’m heading downtown.”\n\nNo food or glass duplication.\n\n6.5–9.0 SECONDS — GETTING READY\n\nMara places the phone on the entrance bench, creating a stable waist-height third-person shot.\n\nShe enters the frame and:\n- Puts on her black leather jacket\n- Slides the tan shoulder bag over her right shoulder\n- Checks that her keys are inside\n- Picks up the phone\n\nShe reaches toward the lens. Her jacket sleeve fills the frame and creates a natural transition.\n\n9.0–12.5 SECONDS — CITY STREET SELFIE\n\nReveal Mara walking along a real Manhattan neighborhood sidewalk in bright afternoon sunlight.\n\nEnvironment:\n- Red-brick apartment buildings\n- Ground-floor cafés and small shops\n- Parked cars\n- One yellow taxi passing in the street\n- Trees with fresh green leaves\n- Ordinary pedestrians\n- Realistic crosswalk and traffic lights\n\nMara holds the phone slightly below eye level and walks at a comfortable pace.\n\nShe says:\n\n“The weather is way too nice to stay inside.”\n\nHer hair moves naturally in the breeze. Sunlight changes subtly as she passes beneath tree shade.\n\nKeep her gait stable and avoid excessive selfie-camera bouncing.\n\n12.5–16.0 SECONDS — CLOTHING STORE\n\nA yellow taxi passes close behind Mara and creates a color-wipe transition into a bright contemporary clothing store.\n\nMara films herself browsing a rack of neutral-colored shirts and lightweight summer jackets.\n\nUse:\n- Over-the-shoulder shot of her hand sliding hangers\n- Mirror shot showing her full outdoor outfit\n- Close-up as she holds a pale blue shirt against herself\n- Brief amused expression when she notices the camera in the mirror\n\nShe carries only one tan shoulder bag.\n\nAt the end, show her leaving with one small kraft-paper shopping bag.\n\nDo not generate readable brand names or price labels.\n\n16.0–19.5 SECONDS — WALKING TO THE CAFÉ\n\nUse a third-person sidewalk shot filmed from approximately four meters ahead.\n\nMara walks toward the camera carrying the small shopping bag. She takes out her phone, checks a message and smiles.\n\nA foreground pedestrian crosses naturally from right to left, creating a brief visual wipe.\n\nCut to Mara opening the door of a warm neighborhood café.\n\nMovement direction remains continuous.\n\n19.5–23.0 SECONDS — CAFÉ WITH ELISE\n\nInside the café, Elise sits at a small wooden table near a window.\n\nMara approaches and gives her a brief natural hug.\n\nUse a combination of:\n- Stable two-shot from a phone placed on the table\n- Close-up of two coffee cups arriving\n- Overhead shot of Mara’s shopping bag beside the chair\n- Short close-up of both women laughing\n\nElise asks:\n\n“So, was the shopping successful?”\n\nMara glances toward the paper bag and replies:\n\n“More successful than planned.”\n\nTheir laughter should feel spontaneous and slightly imperfect.\n\n23.0–26.5 SECONDS — SUNNY PARK WALK\n\nMara lifts the kraft-paper bag briefly past the lens, creating a soft brown wipe transition.\n\nReveal Mara and Elise walking through a large sunny city park.\n\nEnvironment:\n- Green lawn\n- Mature trees\n- Paved walking path\n- People sitting on blankets in the distance\n- Joggers and cyclists remaining far behind\n- Partial city skyline visible through the trees\n- Warm late-afternoon sunlight\n\nElise films Mara for a short third-person shot as Mara walks backward, laughs and gestures toward the park.\n\nCut to Mara’s selfie camera as Elise enters beside her.\n\n26.5–30.0 SECONDS — FRIENDSHIP MOMENT AND SIGN-OFF\n\nMara turns toward Elise and they share a quick warm hug.\n\nKeep the phone in Mara’s extended right hand. The camera naturally shifts closer during the hug but does not become fully blocked.\n\nThey separate and sit side by side on a park bench.\n\nMara looks into the camera and says:\n\n“Honestly, this was exactly the kind of day I needed.”\n\nElise smiles and waves once.\n\nMara reaches her hand toward the lens. Her palm fills the frame naturally and ends the video.\n\nHold no artificial freeze frame.\n\nPERFORMANCE DIRECTION\n\nMara’s delivery should feel conversational rather than scripted.\n\nInclude:\n- Natural pauses\n- Small breaths\n- Occasional glances at the screen\n- Slightly imperfect hand gestures\n- Real blinking\n- Brief laughter\n- Subtle changes in walking speed\n- Hair adjustments caused by wind\n\nAvoid exaggerated influencer expressions, constant wide smiles or overly polished advertising behavior.\n\nCAMERA AND EDITING QUALITY\n\n- Realistic smartphone dynamic range\n- Slight handheld movement\n- Smooth stabilization without floating-camera behavior\n- Consistent left-right screen direction\n- Natural autofocus adjustments\n- Brief realistic exposure adaptation when moving indoors or outdoors\n- Cuts motivated by gestures and foreground wipes\n- No random viewpoint changes\n- No impossible camera positions\n- No excessive lens flare\n- No slow motion\n- No speed ramping\n\nLIGHTING AND COLOR\n\nUse bright, natural late-spring daylight.\n\nApartment:\nSoft neutral morning window light.\n\nStreet:\nClear sunlight with moving tree shadows.\n\nStore and café:\nBalanced practical interior lighting mixed with daylight.\n\nPark:\nWarm but realistic late-afternoon sunlight.\n\nMaintain natural skin tones.\nNo heavy orange filter, teal-and-orange grading, crushed shadows or overexposed windows.\n\nAUDIO\n\nUse realistic vlog audio:\n- Mara and Elise’s natural dialogue\n- Apartment room tone\n- Blender operating briefly\n- City traffic\n- Pedestrian footsteps\n- Clothing-store ambience\n- Quiet café conversation\n- Cups touching the table\n- Park wind and distant voices\n\nOptional very soft original acoustic-pop instrumental beneath the montage portions only.\n\nDialogue must remain clear.\nNo artificial crowd cheering.\nNo narrator.\n\nTEXT AND GRAPHICS\n\nDo not generate word-by-word subtitles or baked-in captions because unstable AI text may reduce realism.\n\nLeave clean lower-frame space so accurate captions can be added during editing.\n\nNo generated title, logos or watermark.\n\nNEGATIVE CONSTRAINTS\n\nNo identity drift, changing face, changing eye color, changing hair length, spontaneous outfit changes, duplicated shopping bags, duplicated drinks, extra arms, deformed selfie arm, extra fingers, phone visible floating in front of the camera, warped mirrors, incorrect reflections, cloned pedestrians, disappearing jacket, changing weather, teleportation, unstable buildings, excessive beauty filter, plastic skin, overexposed face, artificial bokeh, slow motion, speed ramps, cinematic crane shot, drone shot, random third-person camera, subtitles, unreadable text, logos or watermark.\n\nFINAL OUTPUT\n\n30 seconds.\nHorizontal 4:3.\nPhotorealistic lifestyle influencer vlog.\nOne consistent Spanish-American female creator.\nOne consistent female friend.\nReal New York apartment, street, clothing store, café and sunny park.\nNatural selfie and third-person perspectives.\nSmooth motivated transitions.\nBright realistic daylight.\nConversational everyday atmosphere.","imgs":["https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2104441385726377985/img/esHOf-WQfuR3DIZU.jpg"]},{"i":19074,"text":"Style: Epic dark fantasy, ultra-realistic cinematic live-action, massive scale, dramatic storm atmosphere, realistic dragon anatomy, detailed armor, glowing embers, volumetric lightning, powerful orchestral tension.\n\n0–5 SEC — STORM AWAKENING\nA violent nighttime storm fills the sky. Lightning tears through enormous black clouds as a gigantic ancient charcoal-scaled dragon suddenly emerges from the darkness. An armored warrior rides on its back, their cloak violently whipping in the wind. Lightning flashes behind them, creating a powerful heroic silhouette.\n\n5–10 SEC — THROUGH THE STORM\nThe dragon dives at incredible speed between towering storm clouds. Heavy rain strikes the camera as lightning illuminates its enormous wings. Close-up of the warrior gripping glowing ancient reins, their eyes reflecting blue lightning. Each powerful wingbeat creates shockwaves that tear through the clouds.\n\n10–15 SEC — THE BURNING KINGDOM\nThe dragon breaks through the clouds, revealing a devastated medieval kingdom below. Towers collapse into burning streets, fire spreads across rooftops, and thick smoke covers the horizon. The dragon circles above the ruined city and releases a terrifying roar.\n\n15–20 SEC — FINAL DESCENT\nThe dragon folds its wings and dives toward the burning city. Arrows and flaming projectiles rise from below. The warrior draws a legendary sword glowing with intense blue energy, illuminating their armor and the dragon's scales. Lightning strikes behind them as they descend through rain and fire.\n\n20–25 SEC — THE CHARGE\nThe dragon spreads its wings and races toward the massive burning city gate. Smoke, sparks and debris explode around them. The warrior leans forward with the glowing sword raised, while the dragon accelerates directly toward the gate.\n\n25–30 SEC — LEGENDARY ARRIVAL\nThe dragon smashes through the burning gate in a massive explosion of fire, stone and debris. Suddenly everything becomes quiet. The warrior stands beside the dragon among the ruins, overlooking the burning kingdom. Lightning illuminates their silhouettes as embers slowly drift through the darkness. The dragon gives one final powerful roar as the camera pulls back into a vast cinematic aerial shot.\n\nVisual quality: Ultra-photorealistic, cinematic lighting, realistic fire, rain, smoke and debris, detailed creature textures, natural movement, dramatic camera work, seamless continuity, powerful Hollywood dark-fantasy atmosphere.","imgs":["https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2104565134031290368/img/cahpV1nF1JkxVXiX.jpg"]},{"i":19075,"text":"请基于我上传的照片，制作一张独立的 3:4竖版「水下折光双生」海报，画面上下严格 1:1分割。\n上半部分：\n完整保留原始照片，仅做轻微统一调色。\n保持 同一人物、同一张脸、同一动作、同一服装、同一场景、同一机位、同一构图。\n下半部分：\n严格保持上半部分的 人物身份、面部特征、发型、服装、动作、姿态、主体位置、场景结构和构图不变，将同一画面重构为真实的 水下摄影效果。\n加入：\n- 真实水面折射\n- 蓝绿色水下光感\n- 水波折光\n- caustic 波纹光斑\n- 微小气泡\n- 轻微漂浮感\n- 柔和水体景深\n- 真实水下颗粒感\n要求：\n- 主体脸部和核心轮廓仍然清晰可辨\n- 水光必须沿皮肤、衣服、建筑或物体表面自然变化\n- 可以有轻微头发或布料漂浮\n- 整体要像真的在清澈水中拍摄\n- 不是简单加蓝色滤镜\n最终效果像：\n同一张普通照片，突然被水面吞进去了一半。\n禁止：\n- 禁止换脸\n- 禁止改动作\n- 禁止换场景\n- 禁止整张图变成纯蓝滤镜\n- 禁止卡通水波\n- 禁止夸张特效\n- 禁止明显AI感\n- 禁止失去人物真实身份\n\n🔁延伸玩法\n人物照\n最适合做半身照、侧脸照、站姿照。\n普通街拍一下就会变得很梦幻。\n旅行照\n建筑、街道、海边、泳池边都可以。\n会很像“城市沉进海里”的感觉。\n情侣照\n人不变，只让两个人一起进入水下光感。\n很容易出氛围感。\n产品照\n香水、手表、饮料、护肤品特别适合。\n会很像高级广告图。\n\n📌一句话总结\n上传一张普通照片，让AI把它直接拍成水下大片","imgs":["https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HTWuDBMaQAApUv-.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HTWuJiga0AATDxj.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HTWuJieagAAmDGQ.jpg"]},{"i":19076,"text":"Photorealistic high-end Parisian café lifestyle editorial portrait, vertical 4:5 composition. A stylish young woman with long, naturally tousled dark brown hair sits at an elegant outdoor European café table. She wears a sharp tailored black blazer over a modest matte black full-sleeve top with black trousers, creating a sophisticated monochrome look. She wears classic black rectangular wayfarer sunglasses and a refined silver wristwatch.\nShe is seated upright on a classic woven rattan bistro chair with a black-and-cream checkerboard pattern. Her body faces slightly toward the camera while her head is turned clearly toward the left side of the frame, looking away from the camera with a calm, composed expression. She holds an open copy of The New York Times naturally with both hands as if casually reading it.\nIn front of her is a round black café table with a polished gold/brass rim. On the table: a white ceramic cappuccino cup with subtle heart-shaped latte art, a clear glass of water, an elegant printed menu, and a pair of round black sunglasses placed naturally on the tabletop.\nThe setting is an elegant Parisian-style outdoor café, with a large cream/off-white stucco wall behind her and tall white-framed multi-pane windows revealing a softly blurred warm café interior. Additional woven café chairs are visible around her. The background should feel authentic, refined and naturally lived-in rather than staged.\nComposition: medium-to-full body lifestyle shot, subject positioned slightly right of center, generous environmental background, table visible in the foreground, natural perspective, realistic proportions, subtle candid feeling.\nLighting: soft diffused natural daylight, gentle highlights on the hair and face, balanced exposure, warm interior glow visible through the windows, no harsh artificial lighting.\nPhotography: premium fashion magazine editorial photography, authentic candid street-style aesthetic, 85mm lens look, shallow depth of field, soft creamy background bokeh, sharp focus on subject, realistic environmental reflections, natural skin texture, realistic fabric and hair detail, subtle cinematic color grading, high dynamic range, ultra-detailed photorealism, professional DSLR photography.\nImportant: preserve natural anatomy, realistic hands and fingers, realistic newspaper proportions, physically accurate objects and shadows, no excessive retouching, no plastic skin, no cartoon or CGI appearance.","imgs":["https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HTWs0XgbcAA0JOr.jpg"]},{"i":19077,"text":"Create a sophisticated handcrafted travel-art poster of [LANDMARK / CITY / COUNTRY], illustrated entirely with colored pencils and wax crayons on warm ivory paper.\n\nDepict [LANDMARK / CITY / COUNTRY] as if it has been drawn from memory by an exceptionally talented artist — recognizable architecture and proportions, but expressed through energetic imperfect pencil strokes, layered wax-crayon marks, loose cross-hatching, scribbled shading, overlapping colors, and visible hand pressure.\n\nInstead of filling the landmark with flat color, let hundreds of expressive pencil strokes build its form. Allow certain strokes to extend beyond the architectural edges, creating a sense of movement and imagination. Add tiny hand-drawn visual memories around and within the composition: local patterns, plants, birds, windows, streets, clouds, cultural motifs, landscape elements and subtle symbols associated with the place.\n\nUse a limited but vibrant destination-inspired palette: [COLORS]. Keep some areas intentionally unfinished, allowing the ivory paper to remain visible.\n\nAdd small imperfect handwritten-style typography:\n[COUNTRY / CITY]\n[LANDMARK NAME]\n[COORDINATES OR SHORT PHRASE]\n\nThe result should feel like a rare artist’s sketchbook page transformed into a premium contemporary travel poster — playful, tactile, nostalgic, artistic and highly detailed.\n\nVisible colored-pencil grain, wax-crayon texture, imperfect outlines, layered strokes, subtle paper fibers, hand-drawn imperfections, sophisticated composition, strong negative space, no photorealism, no 3D rendering, no glossy digital effects, no people, 4:5 vertical.\n\nAn even more unique variation: “Pencil Explosion”\n\nThe landmark stays recognizable in the center, but its colors and pencil strokes progressively break apart into tiny illustrated memories of the city — almost like the drawing is coming alive.\n\nThat would preserve the exact crayon/pencil aesthetic of your reference while giving it a much more original concept.","imgs":["https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HTW8AAPbcAArLrk.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HTW8AAQbYAEZAZ0.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HTW8AAQbIAAOiJ8.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HTW8AAXagAABa7A.jpg"]},{"i":19078,"text":"Create a 30-second high-budget cinematic 3D animated comedy short titled “GAINS — Hamster Gym Bro.” A tiny golden hamster with disproportionately muscular arms, realistic fluffy fur, and a serious bodybuilder attitude trains inside a luxurious human gym. He wears a tiny tank top reading “NO DAYS OFF.” Keep the character, outfit, proportions, and visual style consistent throughout. Premium feature-film animation, expressive faces, cinematic lighting, realistic physics, smooth camera movement, detailed environments, 4K.\n\n[0–4s] — Establishing shot of a modern luxury gym with humans training in the background. The camera slowly drops to floor level, revealing the muscular hamster flexing intensely in front of a huge mirror, taking himself extremely seriously.\n\n[4–8s] — He confidently approaches the dumbbell rack and attempts to lift a full-sized 1 kg dumbbell. It is enormous compared with him. His face turns red, cheeks puff out, and his tiny legs shake. He barely lifts it before dropping it, then casually walks away pretending nothing happened.\n\n[8–12s] — He jumps onto a treadmill and presses START. The belt suddenly accelerates, launching him backward across the floor. He tumbles, immediately gets up, checks if anyone noticed, then returns and lowers the speed with embarrassment.\n\n[12–16s] — At the bench press, he uses two pencils as a miniature barbell with erasers as weights. He struggles dramatically through several reps while a smaller hamster wearing glasses acts as his spotter, helping with one finger while pretending to be professional.\n\n[16–20s] — He notices a woman doing yoga and attempts downward dog on a tiny mat beside her. His round body barely forms the pose, becoming a trembling furry lump. Despite struggling, he holds it with fierce determination.\n\n[20–23s] — At the smoothie bar, he orders a protein shake. The blender is enormous compared with him, while his finished shake arrives in a tiny thimble. He chugs it, slams the thimble down, wipes his mouth, and lets out a tiny burp that echoes dramatically.\n\n[23–27s] — In the locker-room doorway, he puts in tiny earbuds and walks toward the camera in exaggerated slow motion. Dramatic backlighting and imaginary wind make his fur flow like a bodybuilding hero.\n\n[27–30s] — Outside the gym, he approaches a tiny hot-pink Barbie-style Jeep. He presses the key fob, the headlights flash, and he climbs inside. The engine roars unexpectedly. He peels away dramatically, completely proud of himself.\n\nCUT TO BLACK.\n\nStyle: cinematic premium 3D animation, realistic fur, exaggerated muscular hamster, expressive facial animation, polished feature-film quality, dynamic camera movement, detailed gym environment, comedic timing, believable physics with playful exaggeration, cinematic depth of field, volumetric lighting, 4K.\n\nAudio: energetic workout music, realistic gym ambience, comedic impacts, treadmill sounds, hamster grunts and squeaks, tiny burp echo, and an exaggerated toy Jeep engine. No dialogue.","imgs":["https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2104898540938100736/img/w-92NpsQBbf0WmHg.jpg"]},{"i":19079,"text":"Using the supplied first frame as the exact opening image, create a 20-second horizontal 4:3 ultra-photorealistic autumn fashion film.\n\nCORE CONCEPT\n\nYuna Bell remains lying on the same rug beneath a continuously rotating walnut ceiling fan.\n\nThe fixed overhead camera never moves.\n\nEvery time one fan blade physically sweeps across Yuna’s body, her outfit changes seamlessly into the next established autumn look. The blade is the only transition device.\n\nThe effect must resemble an expertly planned practical in-camera fashion transition, not a magical body transformation.\n\nIDENTITY LOCK\n\nPreserve Yuna’s exact:\n- Face\n- Eye shape\n- Beauty mark\n- Skin tone\n- Hair color\n- Hair length\n- Body proportions\n- Hand structure\n- Age impression\n\nHer body remains in the same location and orientation throughout the video.\n\nOnly these elements may change during fan-blade transitions:\n- Clothing\n- Shoes\n- Handbag\n- Jewelry\n- Minor editorial pose details\n\nDo not morph her face or body.\n\nCAMERA LOCK\n\n- Fixed 90-degree overhead camera\n- Horizontal 4:3\n- No cuts\n- No camera movement\n- No zoom\n- No rotation\n- No reframing\n- No focus breathing\n- No angle changes\n- No slow motion\n- Real-time fan rotation\n\nFAN CONTINUITY\n\nUse one three-blade walnut ceiling fan rotating clockwise at a constant moderate speed.\n\nThe fan must:\n- Preserve the same blade shape and wood texture\n- Maintain a fixed central axis\n- Rotate at constant speed\n- Cast a consistent moving shadow\n- Pass between the camera and Yuna\n- Create exactly three complete wardrobe transitions\n\nEach transition occurs only behind the passing blade. The new clothing is revealed progressively at the blade’s trailing edge.\n\nNo dissolve, flash, smoke, particles, digital glitch or body morphing.\n\n0.0–3.5 SECONDS — LOOK 1\n\nContinue directly from the first frame.\n\nYuna lies in LOOK 1.\n\nShe presses the small wooden remote once with her right thumb.\n\nShe makes subtle editorial movements:\n- Turns her chin slightly toward camera-right\n- Extends her left wrist\n- Straightens her right leg\n- Gives a restrained half-smile\n- Returns her eyes directly to the camera\n\nHer cinnamon leather jacket creases naturally beneath her shoulders.\nHer breathing creates a subtle rise and fall in her torso.\n\nThe fan continues rotating overhead.\n\n3.5–5.0 SECONDS — TRANSITION TO LOOK 2\n\nThe first broad walnut blade enters from the lower-left and sweeps clockwise across Yuna’s body.\n\nAs the blade crosses:\n- LOOK 1 disappears only within the area hidden by the blade\n- LOOK 2 is revealed immediately behind the trailing edge\n- Her face, body, hair and physical position remain unchanged\n\nReveal LOOK 2:\n- Oatmeal cable-knit sweater\n- Green-and-cream checked pleated skirt\n- Chocolate tights\n- Burgundy loafers\n- Cream socks\n- Dark green top-handle bag\n- Gold necklace\n\nThe burgundy bag from LOOK 1 becomes the dark green bag only while fully covered by the same blade sweep.\n\nNo accessory may remain duplicated.\n\n5.0–8.0 SECONDS — LOOK 2\n\nYuna now wears LOOK 2 completely.\n\nShe changes pose naturally:\n- Brings both hands lightly together over her waist\n- Bends both knees slightly\n- Tilts her head toward camera-left\n- Smooths the edge of the pleated skirt with two fingers\n- Maintains direct upward eye contact\n\nThe cable-knit sweater compresses realistically against the rug.\nThe skirt pleats spread naturally around her hips.\n\nThe fan shadow moves consistently over her face and clothing.\n\n8.0–9.5 SECONDS — TRANSITION TO LOOK 3\n\nA second fan blade sweeps across the frame from upper-left toward lower-right as part of the same clockwise rotation.\n\nBehind the blade, reveal LOOK 3:\n- Muted plum asymmetric knit top\n- Oversized charcoal wool blazer\n- Taupe wide-leg trousers\n- Pointed black ankle boots\n- Oxblood rectangular handbag\n- Sculptural gold earrings\n\nThe pleated skirt and tights disappear only under blade occlusion.\nThe wide-leg trousers emerge with correct continuity around both legs.\n\nYuna’s legs, knees and feet remain in the same anatomical positions.\n\n9.5–13.0 SECONDS — LOOK 3\n\nYuna performs a more structured editorial pose:\n\n- Extends her left leg\n- Bends her right knee outward slightly\n- Places her left hand on the blazer lapel\n- Moves her right hand beside the oxblood bag\n- Turns her face back toward the camera\n- Gives a composed, serious expression\n\nThe blazer spreads naturally over the rug.\nThe wide trousers retain realistic folds and fabric weight.\nThe handbag stays beside her right hip.\n\nNo item floats or slides without contact.\n\n13.0–14.5 SECONDS — TRANSITION TO LOOK 4\n\nThe third walnut fan blade passes over Yuna from lower-right toward upper-left.\n\nReveal LOOK 4 behind its trailing edge:\n- Moss-green fitted cardigan\n- Chocolate satin camisole\n- Espresso leather midi skirt\n- Charcoal socks\n- Burgundy heeled loafers\n- Cherry-red handbag\n- Narrow charcoal headband\n- Gold index-finger ring\n\nThe charcoal blazer, trousers, boots and oxblood bag disappear completely beneath the blade before the new items appear.\n\nHair remains the same length and arrangement except for the charcoal headband being added during full blade occlusion.\n\n14.5–18.0 SECONDS — LOOK 4\n\nYuna now wears LOOK 4 completely.\n\nShe performs the final pose adjustment:\n- Extends both legs diagonally toward camera-right\n- Crosses her ankles\n- Places the cherry-red handbag beside her left waist\n- Raises her right hand near her collarbone\n- Places her left arm above her head\n- Turns her chin slightly toward camera-left\n- Returns her eyes directly to the camera\n\nShe gives a very subtle confident smile.\n\nThe leather skirt shows restrained natural highlights.\nThe satin camisole responds softly to her breathing.\nThe cardigan fibers remain visible.\n\n18.0–20.0 SECONDS — FINAL HOLD\n\nYuna becomes completely still in LOOK 4.\n\nOnly the following continue moving:\n- Natural breathing\n- One or two loose hair strands\n- Rotating ceiling fan\n- Soft moving fan shadow\n- Subtle sunlight variation\n\nThe fan completes another partial rotation but does not trigger an additional outfit change.\n\nEnd with Yuna looking directly upward, framed symmetrically on the autumn rug.\n\nHold the final image for the last half-second.\n\nMOTION QUALITY\n\n- Real-time movement only\n- Subtle editorial posing\n- Natural joint movement\n- Accurate finger anatomy\n- Realistic breathing\n- Physically correct fabric compression\n- Consistent fan speed\n- Stable room geometry\n- No sliding body\n- No changing body scale\n- No sudden pose teleportation\n\nFASHION MATERIAL QUALITY\n\nRender materials distinctly:\n\n- Cable knit: visible yarn and soft thickness\n- Leather jacket: matte grain and natural creases\n- Wool blazer: dense soft texture\n- Satin camisole: controlled highlights\n- Leather skirt: structured weight and subtle reflection\n- Tights: opaque woven appearance\n- Handbags: firm construction and believable straps\n- Shoes: stable shape, soles and closures\n\nLIGHTING AND COLOR\n\nMaintain consistent late-afternoon sunlight throughout.\n\nColor palette:\n- Walnut brown\n- Burnt sienna\n- Burgundy\n- Moss green\n- Charcoal\n- Oatmeal\n- Muted plum\n\nUse premium but natural autumn color grading.\nPreserve real skin tone.\nNo extreme orange cast or crushed shadows.\n\nAUDIO\n\nUse subtle realistic apartment sound:\n- Quiet ceiling-fan motor\n- Soft blade movement through air\n- Remote-button click\n- Gentle clothing rustle\n- Low room ambience\n\nOptional minimal original ambient fashion soundtrack at very low volume.\n\nNo dialogue.\nNo narration.\nNo transition sound effects.\nNo camera shutter sounds.\n\nNEGATIVE CONSTRAINTS\n\nNo cuts, camera movement, zoom, camera rotation, angle change, morphing face, changing body, identity drift, changing hair length, duplicated clothing, overlapping outfits, extra shoes, duplicated handbags, disappearing limbs, extra fingers, warped hands, broken legs, floating accessories, sliding props, unstable rug pattern, changing floorboards, fan changing shape, fan changing direction, inconsistent fan speed, blade passing through the body, dissolve transition, flash transition, smoke, particles, digital glitch, excessive fabric movement, artificial wind, beauty filter, text, subtitles, labels, logos or watermark.\n\nFINAL OUTPUT\n\n20 seconds.\nHorizontal 4:3.\nOne fixed 90-degree overhead shot.\nOne consistent adult female model.\nFour original premium autumn outfits.\nExactly three fan-blade wardrobe transitions.\nWarm realistic apartment.\nPhotorealistic fabric, skin and lighting.\nPremium editorial fashion-campaign realism.","imgs":["https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2104945892667338752/img/glRUGZL6C9ByKG6L.jpg"]}];